{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"adaaae72-821f-4e8e-ac22-680bf6e7ab58","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:41:18.620Z","version":"2.1.303","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"8088399433e7c29a09f236c563095ccd40123a439eda5f28074997943c361eb3","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"d6371fa3-c3cf-48d3-af84-f6362d4e73cf","keep":356,"tail":["5880faf8e11de2a8de576d6e1d9d06d9ef7c5b9d8899f55c4cb18eba7f600039","954320c0e676527fb1d4c7b75611be17586cb5982630cc37731c107ac5a997ee","4b8bd9022e1f1d78333fcd370681ee79d1655b97a52c14e0e30360c64fe2dca4"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",358,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f87d367e4e6e34b96075a05793d79918f529b9e8322e2ad8711e629aac71a5a1"}
{"parentUuid":"0daed485-d62c-4fe8-91bb-02b7570358d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAkAhqY5aHrcHS7FE3Fy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to spin up fresh Haiku 5.5 subagents with effort set to xhigh and no prior context, using the general-purpose agent type so they have full tool access including the Paper MCP tools. Since they'll have no history, each prompt needs to be fully self-contained, and I should figure out what exactly they're meant to optimize—likely something related to Paper nodes.\n\nSince each Haiku agent could mess things up, I want a safety net: have each agent duplicate its artboard as a backup before editing, work on the original, then compare before/after screenshots to confirm no visual drift. If something's off, I'd rather restore from backup than trust an undo that doesn't really exist in the API, so I'll have agents leave backups named clearly and placed far below the originals for me to verify and clean up myself afterward.\n\nI'm splitting the work across four agents by section, grouping node IDs so each owns a distinct set of artboards, and I need to flag known gotchas — margin isn't supported, absolute positioning gets dropped inside certain subtrees, the background shorthand can wreck layout, and they must call get_guide first and finish_working_on_nodes when done. I also want to clarify what \"optimize\" means here (flattening wrappers, converting absolute to flex where safe, swapping hardcoded colors for tokens, consistent naming) while warning them specifically not to delete the opacity-0 sidebar mascot node since it's an intentional animation state, not clutter.\n\nNow I'm laying out backup coordinates for each agent so their staging copies don't collide spatially, then setting up to run all four in parallel in the background with the right fileId and page reference before writing out the actual prompt template for them.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":259488,"output_tokens":7876,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":993},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7876,"cache_read_input_tokens":259488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14426,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgAkAhL2mRx3Q2mnAoQQ1","requestRef":"adaaae72-821f-4e8e-ac22-680bf6e7ab58","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b2fba35-62a4-4d6a-96b0-8f46d4a08c70","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:41:35.580Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"2b2fba35-62a4-4d6a-96b0-8f46d4a08c70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAkAhqY5aHrcHS7FE3Fy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kh9TPWJ2EmX59TSnd3RsFa","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit Paper screens 1.1–1.3","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are cleaning up the internal structure of some UI mockups in Paper (a design tool you control through the `mcp__paper__*` tools). The mockups are about to be implemented in a real app, and developers will read the layer structure and styles via `get_jsx` / `get_computed_styles`. Your job: make the layer tree and CSS as clean and simple as possible WITHOUT changing how anything looks. Zero visual, layout or structural regressions is the hard requirement; cleanliness is secondary.\n\n## Scope\n- Paper file id: `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page id `p-6-0`.\n- You own ONLY these artboards (other agents are editing other artboards on the same page at the same time, so never touch anything else):\n  - `3YC-0` \"1.1 Library\"\n  - `437-0` \"1.2 Search · drops in\"\n  - `484-0` \"1.3 Search · query pinned\"\n\n## Required procedure\n1. Call `mcp__paper__get_guide({ topic: \"paper-mcp-instructions\" })` first and follow it.\n2. BACKUP before editing: `duplicate_nodes` each owned artboard, rename the copy to `BACKUP · <original name>`, and move it with `update_styles` to `top: 6000px` with `left` of 0px, 1520px and 3040px respectively. Never edit the backups.\n3. For each artboard, take a \"before\" `get_screenshot` (scale 1) and read its structure with `get_tree_summary`, `get_jsx` and `get_computed_styles`.\n4. Make careful, incremental cleanups (see below). After every few edits, screenshot again and compare against \"before\". If ANYTHING differs (position, size, spacing, colour, clipping, text wrapping, layering), undo that edit immediately by restoring the previous style values.\n5. At the end, take final screenshots at scale 1 and compare them to the backups pixel-for-pixel by eye, region by region (sidebar, toolbar, grid, overlays). Call `finish_working_on_nodes`.\n6. Leave the backups in place (the coordinator will verify and remove them). If an artboard ended up broken and you cannot fix it, say so plainly in your report instead of hiding it.\n\n## What to clean up\n- Remove redundant wrapper frames that add nothing (a single-child frame with no styles that affect layout or paint). Only if removing it provably changes nothing.\n- Replace leftover `position: absolute` + hardcoded left/top inside flex layouts with equivalent flex layout ONLY when the result is identical. Absolute positioning that is genuinely needed (overlays, scrims, floating bars, fades) stays.\n- Remove dead or contradictory styles (e.g. width set alongside flex-grow that ignores it, duplicated properties, zero-width borders, transparent backgrounds that do nothing).\n- Where a hardcoded colour or radius exactly equals a token value, switch it to the token: `--library-canvas #0C0C0B`, `--library-surface #161412`, `--library-surface-raised #1B1917`, `--library-border #262221`, `--library-text #E5DDD2`, `--library-muted #8D867C`, `--library-accent #B0714F`, `--search-radius 20px`, `--sidebar-radius 14px`, `--toggle-radius 12px`, `--button-radius-normal 9px`, `--library-radius-overlay 24px`. Exact matches only, never approximate.\n- Give layers clear, consistent names (e.g. \"Frame\" → \"Nav row · Everything\"). Repeated items should share a naming pattern.\n- Make repeated elements (sidebar rows, toolbar pills, cards of the same type) use consistent style properties.\n\n## Do NOT\n- Do not change any visible colour, size, spacing, font, text content, radius, image, or z-order.\n- Do not delete nodes with opacity 0 or that look invisible; they may represent animation states.\n- Do not use the `background` shorthand in update_styles (it has been seen to wipe layout properties); use backgroundColor / backgroundImage individually. Paper does not support `margin`; use padding/gap/spacers.\n- `position:absolute` inside a `write_html` subtree can be silently dropped, so prefer `update_styles`, `move_nodes`, `rename_nodes`, `delete_nodes` over rewriting HTML.\n- Do not touch any artboard outside your scope.\n\n## Report\nReply with a short list per artboard: what you changed, anything you deliberately left alone and why, and whether the final screenshot matched the backup exactly. Be honest about any difference.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":259488,"output_tokens":7876,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":993},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7876,"cache_read_input_tokens":259488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Kh9TPWJ2EmX59TSnd3RsFa":{"description":"Audit Paper screens 1.1–1.3","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are cleaning up the internal structure of some UI mockups in Paper (a design tool you control through the `mcp__paper__*` tools). The mockups are about to be implemented in a real app, and developers will read the layer structure and styles via `get_jsx` / `get_computed_styles`. Your job: make the layer tree and CSS as clean and simple as possible WITHOUT changing how anything looks. Zero visual, layout or structural regressions is the hard requirement; cleanliness is secondary.\n\n## Scope\n- Paper file id: `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page id `p-6-0`.\n- You own ONLY these artboards (other agents are editing other artboards on the same page at the same time, so never touch anything else):\n  - `3YC-0` \"1.1 Library\"\n  - `437-0` \"1.2 Search · drops in\"\n  - `484-0` \"1.3 Search · query pinned\"\n\n## Required procedure\n1. Call `mcp__paper__get_guide({ topic: \"paper-mcp-instructions\" })` first and follow it.\n2. BACKUP before editing: `duplicate_nodes` each owned artboard, rename the copy to `BACKUP · <original name>`, and move it with `update_styles` to `top: 6000px` with `left` of 0px, 1520px and 3040px respectively. Never edit the backups.\n3. For each artboard, take a \"before\" `get_screenshot` (scale 1) and read its structure with `get_tree_summary`, `get_jsx` and `get_computed_styles`.\n4. Make careful, incremental cleanups (see below). After every few edits, screenshot again and compare against \"before\". If ANYTHING differs (position, size, spacing, colour, clipping, text wrapping, layering), undo that edit immediately by restoring the previous style values.\n5. At the end, take final screenshots at scale 1 and compare them to the backups pixel-for-pixel by eye, region by region (sidebar, toolbar, grid, overlays). Call `finish_working_on_nodes`.\n6. Leave the backups in place (the coordinator will verify and remove them). If an artboard ended up broken and you cannot fix it, say so plainly in your report instead of hiding it.\n\n## What to clean up\n- Remove redundant wrapper frames that add nothing (a single-child frame with no styles that affect layout or paint). Only if removing it provably changes nothing.\n- Replace leftover `position: absolute` + hardcoded left/top inside flex layouts with equivalent flex layout ONLY when the result is identical. Absolute positioning that is genuinely needed (overlays, scrims, floating bars, fades) stays.\n- Remove dead or contradictory styles (e.g. width set alongside flex-grow that ignores it, duplicated properties, zero-width borders, transparent backgrounds that do nothing).\n- Where a hardcoded colour or radius exactly equals a token value, switch it to the token: `--library-canvas #0C0C0B`, `--library-surface #161412`, `--library-surface-raised #1B1917`, `--library-border #262221`, `--library-text #E5DDD2`, `--library-muted #8D867C`, `--library-accent #B0714F`, `--search-radius 20px`, `--sidebar-radius 14px`, `--toggle-radius 12px`, `--button-radius-normal 9px`, `--library-radius-overlay 24px`. Exact matches only, never approximate.\n- Give layers clear, consistent names (e.g. \"Frame\" → \"Nav row · Everything\"). Repeated items should share a naming pattern.\n- Make repeated elements (sidebar rows, toolbar pills, cards of the same type) use consistent style properties.\n\n## Do NOT\n- Do not change any visible colour, size, spacing, font, text content, radius, image, or z-order.\n- Do not delete nodes with opacity 0 or that look invisible; they may represent animation states.\n- Do not use the `background` shorthand in update_styles (it has been seen to wipe layout properties); use backgroundColor / backgroundImage individually. Paper does not support `margin`; use padding/gap/spacers.\n- `position:absolute` inside a `write_html` subtree can be silently dropped, so prefer `update_styles`, `move_nodes`, `rename_nodes`, `delete_nodes` over rewriting HTML.\n- Do not touch any artboard outside your scope.\n\n## Report\nReply with a short list per artboard: what you changed, anything you deliberately left alone and why, and whether the final screenshot matched the backup exactly. Be honest about any difference.","run_in_background":true}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgAkAhL2mRx3Q2mnAoQQ1","requestRef":"adaaae72-821f-4e8e-ac22-680bf6e7ab58","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"75bfbab0-15c5-4d7d-b76c-d1056e374c74","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:41:47.664Z","advisorMode