{"parentUuid":"727f709e-64c6-438c-91de-2fd2f7a2e00d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAkAhqY5aHrcHS7FE3Fy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018MhMSjoe3mNrvg5oxH3gtP","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit Paper screens 3.1–4.1","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are cleaning up the internal structure of some UI mockups in Paper (a design tool you control through the `mcp__paper__*` tools). The mockups are about to be implemented in a real app, and developers will read the layer structure and styles via `get_jsx` / `get_computed_styles`. Your job: make the layer tree and CSS as clean and simple as possible WITHOUT changing how anything looks. Zero visual, layout or structural regressions is the hard requirement; cleanliness is secondary.\n\n## Scope\n- Paper file id: `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page id `p-6-0`.\n- You own ONLY these artboards (other agents are editing other artboards on the same page at the same time, so never touch anything else):\n  - `4XI-0` \"3.1 Settings · Library\" (a library screen with a dimming scrim and a settings sheet on top)\n  - `551-0` \"3.2 Settings · Archive\" (same, archive tab)\n  - `4RN-0` \"4.1 Mascot · search bar travel + states\" (a storyboard board of mascot frames and expression cards)\n\n## Required procedure\n1. Call `mcp__paper__get_guide({ topic: \"paper-mcp-instructions\" })` first and follow it.\n2. BACKUP before editing: `duplicate_nodes` each owned artboard, rename the copy to `BACKUP · <original name>`, and move it with `update_styles` to `top: 9300px` with `left` of 0px, 1520px and 3040px respectively. Never edit the backups.\n3. For each artboard, take a \"before\" `get_screenshot` (scale 1) and read its structure with `get_tree_summary`, `get_jsx` and `get_computed_styles`.\n4. Make careful, incremental cleanups (see below). After every few edits, screenshot again and compare against \"before\". If ANYTHING differs (position, size, spacing, colour, clipping, text wrapping, layering), undo that edit immediately by restoring the previous style values.\n5. At the end, take final screenshots at scale 1 and compare them to the backups by eye, region by region. Call `finish_working_on_nodes`.\n6. Leave the backups in place (the coordinator will verify and remove them). If an artboard ended up broken and you cannot fix it, say so plainly in your report instead of hiding it.\n\n## What to clean up\n- Remove redundant wrapper frames that add nothing (a single-child frame with no styles that affect layout or paint). Only if removing it provably changes nothing.\n- Replace leftover `position: absolute` + hardcoded left/top inside flex layouts with equivalent flex layout ONLY when the result is identical. Absolute positioning that is genuinely needed (the scrim, the settings sheet, overlays, fades) stays.\n- Remove dead or contradictory styles (e.g. width set alongside flex-grow that ignores it, duplicated properties, zero-width borders, transparent backgrounds that do nothing).\n- Where a hardcoded colour or radius exactly equals a token value, switch it to the token: `--library-canvas #0C0C0B`, `--library-surface #161412`, `--library-surface-raised #1B1917`, `--library-border #262221`, `--library-text #E5DDD2`, `--library-muted #8D867C`, `--library-accent #B0714F`, `--search-radius 20px`, `--sidebar-radius 14px`, `--toggle-radius 12px`, `--button-radius-normal 9px`, `--library-radius-overlay 24px`. Exact matches only, never approximate.\n- Give layers clear, consistent names (e.g. \"Frame\" → \"Settings row · Export\"). Repeated items should share a naming pattern.\n- Make repeated elements (rows, tiles, cards, pills) use consistent style properties.\n\n## Do NOT\n- Do not change any visible colour, size, spacing, font, text content, radius, image, or z-order.\n- Do not delete nodes with opacity 0 or that look invisible; they may represent animation states.\n- Do not use the `background` shorthand in update_styles (it has been seen to wipe layout properties); use backgroundColor / backgroundImage individually. Paper does not support `margin`; use padding/gap/spacers.\n- `position:absolute` inside a `write_html` subtree can be silently dropped, so prefer `update_styles`, `move_nodes`, `rename_nodes`, `delete_nodes` over rewriting HTML.\n- Do not touch any artboard outside your scope.\n\n## Report\nReply with a short list per artboard: what you changed, anything you deliberately left alone and why, and whether the final screenshot matched the backup exactly. Be honest about any difference.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":259488,"output_tokens":7876,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":993},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7876,"cache_read_input_tokens":259488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018MhMSjoe3mNrvg5oxH3gtP":{"description":"Audit Paper screens 3.1–4.1","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are cleaning up the internal structure of some UI mockups in Paper (a design tool you control through the `mcp__paper__*` tools). The mockups are about to be implemented in a real app, and developers will read the layer structure and styles via `get_jsx` / `get_computed_styles`. Your job: make the layer tree and CSS as clean and simple as possible WITHOUT changing how anything looks. Zero visual, layout or structural regressions is the hard requirement; cleanliness is secondary.\n\n## Scope\n- Paper file id: `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page id `p-6-0`.\n- You own ONLY these artboards (other agents are editing other artboards on the same page at the same time, so never touch anything else):\n  - `4XI-0` \"3.1 Settings · Library\" (a library screen with a dimming scrim and a settings sheet on top)\n  - `551-0` \"3.2 Settings · Archive\" (same, archive tab)\n  - `4RN-0` \"4.1 Mascot · search bar travel + states\" (a storyboard board of mascot frames and expression cards)\n\n## Required procedure\n1. Call `mcp__paper__get_guide({ topic: \"paper-mcp-instructions\" })` first and follow it.\n2. BACKUP before editing: `duplicate_nodes` each owned artboard, rename the copy to `BACKUP · <original name>`, and move it with `update_styles` to `top: 9300px` with `left` of 0px, 1520px and 3040px respectively. Never edit the backups.\n3. For each artboard, take a \"before\" `get_screenshot` (scale 1) and read its structure with `get_tree_summary`, `get_jsx` and `get_computed_styles`.\n4. Make careful, incremental cleanups (see below). After every few edits, screenshot again and compare against \"before\". If ANYTHING differs (position, size, spacing, colour, clipping, text wrapping, layering), undo that edit immediately by restoring the previous style values.\n5. At the end, take final screenshots at scale 1 and compare them to the backups by eye, region by region. Call `finish_working_on_nodes`.\n6. Leave the backups in place (the coordinator will verify and remove them). If an artboard ended up broken and you cannot fix it, say so plainly in your report instead of hiding it.\n\n## What to clean up\n- Remove redundant wrapper frames that add nothing (a single-child frame with no styles that affect layout or paint). Only if removing it provably changes nothing.\n- Replace leftover `position: absolute` + hardcoded left/top inside flex layouts with equivalent flex layout ONLY when the result is identical. Absolute positioning that is genuinely needed (the scrim, the settings sheet, overlays, fades) stays.\n- Remove dead or contradictory styles (e.g. width set alongside flex-grow that ignores it, duplicated properties, zero-width borders, transparent backgrounds that do nothing).\n- Where a hardcoded colour or radius exactly equals a token value, switch it to the token: `--library-canvas #0C0C0B`, `--library-surface #161412`, `--library-surface-raised #1B1917`, `--library-border #262221`, `--library-text #E5DDD2`, `--library-muted #8D867C`, `--library-accent #B0714F`, `--search-radius 20px`, `--sidebar-radius 14px`, `--toggle-radius 12px`, `--button-radius-normal 9px`, `--library-radius-overlay 24px`. Exact matches only, never approximate.\n- Give layers clear, consistent names (e.g. \"Frame\" → \"Settings row · Export\"). Repeated items should share a naming pattern.\n- Make repeated elements (rows, tiles, cards, pills) use consistent style properties.\n\n## Do NOT\n- Do not change any visible colour, size, spacing, font, text content, radius, image, or z-order.\n- Do not delete nodes with opacity 0 or that look invisible; they may represent animation states.\n- Do not use the `background` shorthand in update_styles (it has been seen to wipe layout properties); use backgroundColor / backgroundImage individually. Paper does not support `margin`; use padding/gap/spacers.\n- `position:absolute` inside a `write_html` subtree can be silently dropped, so prefer `update_styles`, `move_nodes`, `rename_nodes`, `delete_nodes` over rewriting HTML.\n- Do not touch any artboard outside your scope.\n\n## Report\nReply with a short list per artboard: what you changed, anything you deliberately left alone and why, and whether the final screenshot matched the backup exactly. Be honest about any difference.","run_in_background":true}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgAkAhL2mRx3Q2mnAoQQ1","requestRef":"adaaae72-821f-4e8e-ac22-680bf6e7ab58","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"838c1536-110b-4ef5-b067-f0caf0f31705","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:42:21.663Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
