{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:48:55.177Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5877e2570c2c57ea</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0162Ri49Mj6FQgRHTBTcPqkR</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a5877e2570c2c57ea.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit Paper screens 2.3–2.4\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both owned artboards are cleaned up, and the final captures match their backups pixel for pixel. The backups are left in place for you to verify and remove.\n\n**Backups** (untouched, at top 8200px):\n- `BACKUP · 2.3 Item · inkling panel`, left 0px\n- `BACKUP · 2.4 Item · inkling panel · Nearby expanded`, left 1520px\n\n**2.3 Item · inkling panel**\n- Removed the empty logo wrapper frame; the logo sits directly in the header.\n- Swapped exact-match hardcoded colours to tokens: surface, border, text, canvas, accent and muted, on frames, icon strokes and fills, and the logo.\n- Switched the nine 9px nav and space row radii to `--button-radius-normal`.\n- Renamed layers, e.g. \"Nav row · Top of mind\", \"Space row · Kitchen\", \"Icon slot\", \"Icon\", \"Zoom in button\".\n- Left alone: the zoom pill (a genuine overlay, still absolute), the fixed-width icon and count slots (they keep the columns aligned), and the space colour dot for \"Design references\", which is user category data and so stays hardcoded, not the accent token.\n- Near-miss colours left as-is because they are not exact token matches: root `#0A0A09` (canvas is `#0C0C0B`), viewer background `#0D0C0B`, zoom pill `#1B1917EB` (has alpha), and the nav text colours.\n- Also left alone: the viewer well's dot-grid background, which has a stray `t:4-0` token in the `background` value. I did not touch it, but it looks like an artifact worth a look.\n\n**2.4 Item · inkling panel · Nearby expanded**\n- Same logo wrapper removal, token swaps (including the note card and quote card borders and text) and 9px radius swap as above.\n- Renamed the Nearby parts (\"Nearby header\", \"Nearby grid\", \"Nearby column 1–3\") and the cards (\"Quote card\", \"Note card\", \"PDF card\", \"Link card\"). The two cards were previously named \"Dark glowing circles\", which described the background texture rather than the card.\n- Left alone: the quote card text colours and the link card background `#ECE6DC`, since neither matches a token.\n\n**Verification**\n- I pixel-diffed the saved screenshot files. The final 2.4 artboard is byte-identical to its backup and to its pre-edit capture.\n- The final 2.3 artboard matches its backup exactly on a re-capture. One earlier capture of the same state differed only inside the first Nearby image tile. A re-capture of the untouched backup showed the same kind of variance, so I attribute it to image-tile loading, not to the edits.\n- The JSX confirms the token references are in place. Old hexes no longer appear on the surface and border nodes.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>230248</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>54</tool_uses><duration_ms>405051</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
