{"parentUuid":"9136eb5a-8c14-4962-91a4-c79f90c278e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAkxBtmAQQfjcBRcfBrH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking whether var() actually works in SVG presentation attributes like fill—agents 2 and 3 used it on the star element, and agent 4 flagged it as a potential browser issue, but I need to verify whether that's really a spec violation or works fine in practice.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2215,"cache_read_input_tokens":53530,"output_tokens":676,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":213},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2215,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":53530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2215},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4442,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgAkxBaf8dL9rP6MYuYHh","requestRef":"aa0337e9-83e9-4ba6-b363-0c6f4ed74773","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"71a6428b-57c6-4036-9f3e-651cb4a4e9ac","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:51:43.229Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"71a6428b-57c6-4036-9f3e-651cb4a4e9ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAkxBtmAQQfjcBRcfBrH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The agent for 3.1, 3.2 and 4.1 has finished, and it raised something I need to check. On Settings it tried putting design tokens into SVG icon colours, saw the icons break, and reverted. The 2.1–2.4 agents did put tokens into icon colours and report no visible change. When I verify, I'll check every icon on those four screens. If any colour broke, I'll restore the plain colour values on those icons.\n\nOtherwise, Settings and the Mascot board got the same cleanup as the other screens:\n- exact-match colours and corner radii switched to tokens\n- one dead width style removed from a few layers\n- the wrappers around the logo and title removed\n- every layer given a proper name\n\nThe two hidden mascot animation states were left in place. The agent compared by eye and reports all three screens matching their backups.\n\n**Naming issue:** some tokens were applied only because the number happened to match, so the token name doesn't describe the element. Nothing looks different because of it:\n- the 20px corner on the quote, note and PDF cards now uses `--search-radius`\n- the 9px corner on sidebar rows uses `--button-radius-normal`, though the rows aren't buttons\n\nThese are worth fixing with properly named tokens (e.g. a card radius and a row radius) when you build this into the app.\n\nThe 1.1–1.3 agent is still running. After it finishes I'll check every screen against its backup and show you the screenshots."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2215,"cache_read_input_tokens":53530,"output_tokens":676,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":213},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2215,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":53530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2215},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgAkxBaf8dL9rP6MYuYHh","requestRef":"aa0337e9-83e9-4ba6-b363-0c6f4ed74773","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bd3ef9b6-36f4-4e4f-a75f-53e276e7db39","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:51:45.475Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:52:05.596Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a50d9eb53dbf1454e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Kh9TPWJ2EmX59TSnd3RsFa</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a50d9eb53dbf1454e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit Paper screens 1.1–1.3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All three cleaned artboards match their backups exactly at scale 1, so the cleanup changed structure and CSS without any visible change. The file is 01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW (page p-6-0), and it is the only file I touched. The three backups (\"BACKUP · 1.1 Library\", \"BACKUP · 1.2 Search · drops in\", \"BACKUP · 1.3 Search · query pinned\") are still in place and were never edited. I called finish_working_on_nodes on the three artboards.\n\n**1.1 Library**\n- Changed: removed two single-child wrappers (the logo wrapper and the \"Everything\" label wrapper). Renamed about 100 layers. Swapped colours and radii to file tokens where the value matched exactly.\n- Left alone: colours with no exact token match, opacity-0 nodes, and fixed-width icon slots, which keep the columns aligned.\n- Final: identical to backup.\n\n**1.2 Search · drops in**\n- Changed: removed the title wrapper and moved the title text up into the toolbar. Renamed layers. Token swaps on exact matches for radii, borders, fills and strokes. The search bar already used --search-radius, so it was only renamed.\n- Left alone:\n  - The logo wrapper is kept because it is opacity 0 and part of the animation state.\n  - The 20px card radius equals --search-radius, but I left it literal so the token name does not suggest cards are search elements.\n  - The 16px radius on the content well has no matching token.\n  - The top scrim gradient has no exact token match.\n  - No 12px, 14px or 24px radii exist in this artboard.\n- Caught and fixed during the work: two batch updates applied the wrong paint property to two path nodes. I corrected both and verified them in the JSX before finishing.\n- Final: identical to backup.\n\n**1.3 Search · query pinned**\n- Changed: removed the logo, title, query-chip and results-count wrappers, moving their children up. Checked visually after each removal. Renamed layers and applied token swaps on exact matches.\n- Left alone: the same categories as 1.2 (non-token colours, opacity-0 nodes).\n- Final: identical to backup.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The \"identical\" result comes from a SHA256 comparison of the saved scale-1 screenshots of each full artboard. Byte equality means every region matches, so I did not need a separate per-region check.\n- find_nodes does not report SVG child fill or stroke values, and get_computed_styles returns empty objects for SVG children. I verified SVG paint changes through get_jsx only.\n- Two background \"Audit Paper screens\" tasks appeared in this session. They are not part of this cleanup, and I did not read or act on them.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>57316</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>92</tool_uses><duration_ms>617916</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
