{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"bca37f05cd8391817a995d6a07b2e4f8da95adce6613f3e70590adf179581851","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The differences I'm seeing are just resampling noise in a couple photos—chrome, text, and layout are otherwise identical, so this is fine for mockups. One thing to flag for implementation though: SVG presentation attributes like fill don't actually accept var() per spec in browsers, so that'll need to use style or currentColor instead when built.\n\nNow I should clean up by deleting the backups, and since nothing visually changed between rounds I'll just embed the one diff image showing the photo noise rather than building out a full comparison render.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Every difference is resampling noise inside a few photos. The interface itself, text, layout and cards all match the backups, so I'm removing the backups."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015c9pthgNS4YBQMSw4f3apC","name":"mcp__paper__delete_nodes","input":{"fileId":"01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW","nodeIds":["6R8-0","6WG-0","71Y-0","766-0","7BA-0","7FV-0","7KJ-0","7PD-0","7X5-0","85A-0"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01926nmyAkH94KfwQ86MZJxS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -rf /tmp/pdiff /c/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/paper-scripts; rm -f /c/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/paper-jsx-*.txt; echo ok","description":"Delete diff scratch and agent scratch files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
