{"parentUuid":"1a42ed2a-2e4c-4839-9db8-0125ca2ef9b8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"de4738fe-ad9e-417f-a667-4560725564ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Redesign inkling in Paper (mockups only), inspired by resurf.so.\n     - File `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page \"resurf redesign\" `p-6-0`.\n   - Screenshot workflow the user wants after each round:\n     - Export JPG at 1x (files land in `~/Downloads`).\n     - Move them to `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\`.\n     - Show them via `mcp__t3-code__html_render`, which requires a `height` param.\n   - Completed this session:\n     - Haiku audit agents with zero-regression cleanup (verified, backups deleted).\n     - New color tokens and role-based radius tokens that fix the confusing shared names (done).\n   - **Latest request:** \"I want to work a bit on making the distiction between the end of like the file viewing area and the beginning of the side panel better, and I want to focus these efforts on the resurf style frames just for now\".\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Paper MCP call formats:**\n     - `duplicate_nodes` takes `nodes:[{id}]`.\n     - `rename_nodes` takes `updates:[{nodeId,name}]`.\n     - `update_styles` takes `updates:[{nodeIds,styles}]`.\n     - `export` takes `pageId` plus `nodes:{id:[{format,scale}]}`.\n     - `create_tokens` and `set_tokens` (supports `newName`).\n     - `find_nodes` with `filters` `styleValue` (supports tokens and wildcards).\n     - Call `finish_working_on_nodes` when done.\n   - **Paper quirks:**\n     - Never set the `background` shorthand; use `backgroundColor` / `backgroundImage`.\n     - No `margin`.\n     - `position:absolute` inside `write_html` subtrees gets dropped.\n     - `t:4-0` inside a `background` value is Paper's internal token reference, not a bug.\n   - **Existing tokens** (they mirror `src/App.css` `:root`, so don't rename them):\n     - `--library-accent` #B0714F, `--library-border` #262221, `--library-canvas` #0C0C0B\n     - `--library-muted` #8D867C, `--library-surface` #161412, `--library-surface-raised` #1B1917\n     - `--library-text` #E5DDD2, `--small-component` 16px\n     - `--button-radius-normal` 9px, `--library-radius-overlay` 24px, `--search-radius` 20px\n     - `--sidebar-radius` 14px, `--toggle-radius` 12px\n   - **New tokens added this session:**\n     - Colors: `--app-background` #0A0A09, `--library-frame` #0D0C0B, `--library-text-soft` #C9C1B6 (general secondary text), `--nav-label-active` #F0E9DF.\n     - Radii: `--row-radius` 9px, `--tile-radius` 12px, `--frame-radius` 16px, `--card-radius` 20px.\n   - **Current token bindings:**\n     - `--search-radius` is now used only on search bars. That includes the mascot board's \"Bar lifting\".\n     - `--button-radius-normal` has no remaining uses in the redesign.\n     - All 38 cards use `--card-radius`. All 87 rows use `--row-radius`. The Similar tiles use `--tile-radius`.\n     - Library frames, content wells and settings panels use `--frame-radius` (TL/BL corners) and `--library-frame` (bg).\n     - Artboard roots and settings sheets use `--app-background`.\n   - **Intentionally left as literals:** quote/article card colors (type-specific), avatar #2A2521, zoom pill #1B1917EB, mascot \"Icon slot\" 14px.\n   - **Implementation notes for the app:**\n     - Add the new tokens to `App.css`.\n     - In the app, use `currentColor` or CSS instead of `var()` inside SVG `fill`/`stroke` attributes.\n     - Open design question: space pills are 28px tall vs tag pills at 26px.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `src/App.css` lines 13–40 were read only. They hold the `:root` token definitions that match the Paper tokens. Nothing was modified.\n   - **Paper page `p-6-0` layout:**\n     - §1 label `6QK-0`:\n       - 1.1 `3YC-0`, 1.2 `437-0`, 1.3 `484-0` at y 160.\n     - §2 label `6QL-0`:\n       - 2.1 `4D5-0` (0,1460): sidebar `4D6-0`; frame `6QC-0` holding viewer `4FQ-0` and inspector `4GG-0` (width 320, paddingLeft 18, paddingRight 16).\n       - 2.2 `5PB-0` (1520,1460).\n       - 2.3 `4KE-0` (3040,1460).\n       - 2.4 `5UE-0` (4560,1460).\n     - §3 label `6QM-0`:\n       - 3.1 `4XI-0`, 3.2 `551-0` at y 2760.\n     - §4 label `6QN-0`:\n       - 4.1 `4RN-0` at (0,4060).\n   - **Structure of frame `6QC-0` (2.1):**\n     - bg `var(--library-frame)`.\n     - 1px `--library-border` on top, left and bottom; TL/BL radius `var(--frame-radius)`.\n     - `display:flex`, `paddingTop` 8px.\n   - Viewer `4FQ-0` style: `background: 'radial-gradient(circle, rgb(42,38,35) 1px, transparent 1.2px) 0% 0% / 18px 18px transparent'`, flex column, flexGrow 1.\n   - The inspector `4GG-0` previously had no separator from the viewer.\n   - **New variants**, duplicates of 2.1 at y 1460:\n     - **`89Q-0` \"2.1a Split · hairline\"** (x 6080): inspector `89S-0` got `borderLeft: 1px solid var(--library-border)`.\n     - **`8ET-0` \"2.1b Split · panel matches sidebar\"** (x 7600): inspector `8EV-0` got `backgroundColor: var(--app-background)`, so the panel bookends the viewer with the sidebar tone.\n     - **`8JW-0` \"2.1c Split · viewer as inset stage\"** (x 9120):\n       - Frame `8JX-0` got `paddingLeft` 8px and `paddingBottom` 8px.\n       - Viewer `8LP-0` got `borderRadius` 14px, a 1px solid `var(--library-border)` border, and `backgroundColor` #121110.\n   - **Exported JPGs** are in the chat-images `resurf-redesign` folder:\n     - `split0.jpg` (original 2.1)\n     - `splitA.jpg`\n     - `splitB.jpg`\n     - `splitC.jpg`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **PIL import:** `python -I` couldn't import PIL. I reran without `-I`.\n   - **Moved user files:** `mv ~/Downloads/*.png` swept up unrelated user PNGs (\"A · Slide…\", \"B · Slide…\"). I immediately moved everything except my 20 exports back with `mv -n`. Lesson: move only the specific exported filenames.\n   - **Wrong token name:** I first named `#C9C1B6` as `--nav-label`, but it's used broadly (metadata, tags, headings). I renamed it to `--library-text-soft`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Audit verification:**\n     - 2.1, 2.2, 2.4, 3.1, 3.2 and 4.1 were byte-identical to their backups.\n     - 1.1, 1.2, 1.3 and 2.3 differed only by photo resampling noise inside image tiles.\n     - The backups (`6R8`, `6WG`, `71Y`, `766`, `7BA`, `7FV`, `7KJ`, `7PD`, `7X5`, `85A`) were deleted, along with the scratch dirs `/tmp/pdiff`, `Temp/paper-scripts` and `paper-jsx-*.txt`.\n   - **Token rebinding:** verified via `find_nodes`. Spot screenshots of 5PB-0 and 551-0 looked unchanged.\n\n6. All user messages (this session after the prior summary):\n   - \"get a few haiku 5.5 subagents on xhigh with no context of what we were doing to audit each of the pages and optimize their under the hood css and js layouts or whatever before me implement this straight into the app. but its important they dont break any of the ui layout functionally or structurally or visually, no regressions just an optimized and clean code as much as you can get\"\n   - \"make new color tokens then. find a way to fix confusing token names for things that have the same value without making a mess of things again\"\n   - \"I want to work a bit on making the distiction between the end of like the file viewing area and the beginning of the side panel better, and I want to focus these efforts on the resurf style frames just for now\"\n   - Standing constraints from AGENTS.md:\n     - Don't commit artifacts.\n     - Don't write to the live library.\n     - Don't spawn agents unless the user asks.\n     - Mockups only, no app code changes.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Show the four split-comparison screenshots to the user via `html_render` (with `height`), with a brief description of each variant, and ask which direction they prefer.\n   - Once the user picks, apply the chosen treatment to the resurf-style frames: 2.1 `4D5-0` and 2.2 `5PB-0`, whose inspector is `5PC-0` inside frame `6QG-0`, viewer `5R3-0`. Then clean up the unused variants.\n   - Call `finish_working_on_nodes` when done.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - I made three variants for the viewer/side-panel distinction on the resurf-style 2.1 frame:\n     - (a) a hairline left border on the panel\n     - (b) the panel background set to `--app-background`, matching the sidebar\n     - (c) the viewer as an inset rounded \"stage\": 8px padding, 14px radius, border, #121110 bg\n   - I screenshot-checked b and c; both look fine.\n   - I exported the original and all three variants as JPGs and moved them to `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\` as `split0.jpg`, `splitA.jpg`, `splitB.jpg` and `splitC.jpg`.\n   - `finish_working_on_nodes` has not yet been called for the new variant artboards.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Render a comparison page via `mcp__t3-code__html_render` (include `height`) showing `split0`, `splitA`, `splitB` and `splitC` with labels: Current, Hairline, Panel matches sidebar, Viewer as inset stage.\n   - Call `finish_working_on_nodes`.\n   - Give a short recommendation and ask the user which variant to apply to 2.1/2.2. This serves the user's request: \"making the distiction between the end of like the file viewing area and the beginning of the side panel better… focus these efforts on the resurf style frames just for now\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"dbfcf9d3-b3db-4f7a-9f29-9f140e381d52","timestamp":"2026-10-19T05:24:28.627Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":28},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
