{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"8b1a9c69-9f69-491a-83f3-f4dc2cf71ff3","timestamp":"2026-10-19T06:20:18.782Z","version":"2.1.303","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"393849d7c89755282473547105e9b0e84221e1094921669c601bb40892e020c7","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"low"}},"base":"ede3e920-af44-4fb8-b52d-20b070543bef","keep":50,"tail":["f7183800a1805ddecca170b8f2f1722e5a9e90d1bae52ac4e6557f60b3db04c0","b3d23b862717113f3f9d28847b3c62f69ba5e1aaebb5bbfa9fb3ad55c0bfc76e","e299e689347d8d379feeda50b00caa45630e374550ac2f37e92f252f398cae4f"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",52,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"98029565590669ecddab4fbf6219cf83bd2403c0507df41d68baac85e3f0fbe5"}
{"parentUuid":"500e26fa-d0c5-420d-a21f-b683312f3159","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgB7SgushtqXHj2uZhEma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"My honest take is cool but cautious — live WebGPU refraction of content behind a moving element means continuous GPU work while the grid scrolls underneath, which conflicts with the performance guidelines. I'd recommend using it sparingly on just a couple floating surfaces like a search bar or zoom pill, or faking the effect with CSS backdrop-filter and SVG displacement instead.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_read_input_tokens":67343,"output_tokens":847,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":232},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":484,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":67343,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":484},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8859,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgB7SgdWBraQvbMjVFsSJ","requestRef":"8b1a9c69-9f69-491a-83f3-f4dc2cf71ff3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"81729c67-f836-4082-81e1-11590080df73","timestamp":"2026-10-19T06:20:29.323Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"81729c67-f836-4082-81e1-11590080df73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgB7SgushtqXHj2uZhEma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm in, as long as it's an accent on one or two surfaces and not the whole interface.\n\n**Why I'd hold back on the library itself:**\n- **GPU cost:** it renders live glass with WebGPU, redrawing whatever sits behind the glass. In inkling that's the card grid, which moves every time the user scrolls, so the GPU would be busy constantly. AGENTS.md specifically rules out effects that keep repainting, because they peg the GPU on high-refresh displays.\n- **Very early:** it's at version 0.0.2. It also needs React 19 or later, and it stops rendering if no WebGPU adapter is available. That's a real risk on older Windows laptops.\n- **Competes with the content:** inkling is a calm library of other people's images. Heavy refraction everywhere would pull attention away from the things people actually saved.\n\n**What I'd do instead:** build the glass ourselves with CSS and SVG filters, using `backdrop-filter` with a little edge distortion and a bright rim. That gets most of the look. Electron runs on Chromium, which supports this well. It's also cheaper because the browser already handles it as normal compositing, and it adds no new dependency.\n\n**Where it would look good:** the things that float over scrolling content:\n- **Search bar:** the strongest candidate.\n- **Zoom pill:** it already uses a translucent `#1B1917EB` background, so it's halfway to glass.\n- **Card overlay:** the bar on a card when you hover over it.\n- **Possibly the mascot's spot:** the place where the mascot sits.\n\nPanels, the sidebar and the side panel should stay solid.\n\nPaper can't show real refraction, so the useful next step is an interactive HTML prototype like the motion one. It would show the search bar and zoom pill as glass over a scrolling grid of cards, with an intensity slider. Want me to build it?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_read_input_tokens":67343,"output_tokens":847,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":232},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":484,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":67343,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":484},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgB7SgdWBraQvbMjVFsSJ","requestRef":"8b1a9c69-9f69-491a-83f3-f4dc2cf71ff3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"163ff67d-3f2a-476b-871a-9e32565d7f41","timestamp":"2026-10-19T06:20:29.349Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
