{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"163ff67d-3f2a-476b-871a-9e32565d7f41","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","isMeta":false,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:40:59.919Z","uuid":"986d7284-bc9c-4312-a5d2-8f8d07919f8e","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"manual","preTokens":69125,"durationMs":29284,"preCompactDiscoveredTools":["WebFetch","WebSearch","mcp__paper__create_artboard","mcp__paper__create_page","mcp__paper__create_tokens","mcp__paper__delete_nodes","mcp__paper__duplicate_nodes","mcp__paper__export","mcp__paper__find_nodes","mcp__paper__finish_working_on_nodes","mcp__paper__get_basic_info","mcp__paper__get_children","mcp__paper__get_fill_image","mcp__paper__get_font_family_info","mcp__paper__get_guide","mcp__paper__get_jsx","mcp__paper__get_node_info","mcp__paper__get_screenshot","mcp__paper__get_tokens","mcp__paper__get_tree_summary","mcp__paper__list_resources","mcp__paper__move_nodes","mcp__paper__rename_nodes","mcp__paper__set_text_content","mcp__paper__set_tokens","mcp__paper__update_styles","mcp__paper__write_html","mcp__t3-code__device_screenshot","mcp__t3-code__html_preview","mcp__t3-code__html_render","mcp__t3-code__preview_click","mcp__t3-code__preview_evaluate","mcp__t3-code__preview_open","mcp__t3-code__preview_resize","mcp__t3-code__preview_scroll","mcp__t3-code__preview_snapshot"],"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"81729c67-f836-4082-81e1-11590080df73","anchorUuid":"c2cfa7e1-3339-4c4e-b386-47909d3c2f1d","tailUuid":"163ff67d-3f2a-476b-871a-9e32565d7f41"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"c2cfa7e1-3339-4c4e-b386-47909d3c2f1d","uuids":["81729c67-f836-4082-81e1-11590080df73","163ff67d-3f2a-476b-871a-9e32565d7f41"],"allUuids":["81729c67-f836-4082-81e1-11590080df73","163ff67d-3f2a-476b-871a-9e32565d7f41"]},"postTokens":4811,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":1006385},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"986d7284-bc9c-4312-a5d2-8f8d07919f8e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f4fcb119-60cd-4d7e-8750-0df34b39cf1e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Redesign inkling in Paper, mockups only, inspired by resurf.so.\n     - File `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page `p-6-0`.\n   - Screenshot workflow:\n     - Export JPG at 1x; files land in `~/Downloads`.\n     - Move ONLY the specific exported filenames into `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\`.\n     - Show them via `mcp__t3-code__html_render`, which needs a `height` param.\n   - Done this session:\n     - Improved the separation between the viewer and the side panel on the Resurf-style frames.\n     - The user chose variant **c** (viewer as an inset stage) after seeing an animated prototype. It's applied to 2.1 and 2.2.\n   - **Latest request:** the user asked what I think about adding https://github.com/Glass-HQ/liquid-glass, something similar, or a from-scratch version for the redesign (\"just because why not we yoloing anyway right and i just thought it was cool\").\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Paper MCP call formats:**\n     - `update_styles` takes `updates:[{nodeIds,styles}]`.\n     - `export` takes `pageId` plus `nodes:{id:[{format,scale}]}`.\n     - `delete_nodes`.\n     - Call `finish_working_on_nodes` when done.\n     - Never set the `background` shorthand.\n   - **Tokens:**\n     - Colors: `--library-border` #262221, `--library-frame` #0D0C0B, `--app-background` #0A0A09.\n     - Radii: `--card-radius` 20px, `--frame-radius` 16px, `--row-radius` 9px, `--tile-radius` 12px, `--search-radius` 20px (search bars only).\n     - These mirror `src/App.css` `:root`. The new tokens still need adding to App.css when implementing.\n   - **Motion direction for the app:**\n     - A FLIP or shared-element morph from the card into the stage, with the same radius on both so the corners stay continuous.\n     - The panel slides in independently (translateX 28px plus a fade, delayed about 25%).\n     - The grid fades and scales to 0.97.\n     - Easing `cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)`, about 450ms recommended for the real app; the prototype used 700ms.\n     - In the app, use transforms rather than animating layout.\n   - **liquid-glass facts:**\n     - React 19+, web and Electron, built with \"vgpu\", requires WebGPU (HTTPS or localhost).\n     - MIT licensed, version 0.0.2, known Safari issues, no performance notes.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Paper edits (2.1 `4D5-0`):** frame `6QC-0` got paddingLeft and paddingBottom of 8px. Viewer `4FQ-0` got:\n     - borderRadius `var(--card-radius)`\n     - borderTop/Right/Bottom/Left `1px solid var(--library-border)`\n     - backgroundColor `#121110`\n     - The dot-grid backgroundImage is still there.\n   - **Paper edits (2.2 `5PB-0`):** frame `6QG-0` and viewer `5R3-0` got the same changes.\n   - **Deleted:** variant artboards `89Q-0`, `8ET-0`, `8JW-0`.\n   - **Screenshots** in the chat-images folder: `split0/A/B/C.jpg`, `final21.jpg`, `final22.jpg`.\n   - No app code was changed.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Earlier: an over-broad `mv` of PNGs out of Downloads. Fixed, and since then I move only exact filenames.\n   - I showed final21/final22 without inspecting them first and told the user so. The possible issue to watch is how the dot grid looks on the darker #121110 stage in 2.2.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The user was undecided between a and c. The animated HTML prototype comparing open and close motion settled it in favour of c.\n\n6. All user messages (since the last summary):\n   - \"can I see some screenshots pls\"\n   - \"idk, when I think about the animations I might could or want to have for opening and closing this ui for an items details I cant pick between a and c. wdyt??\"\n   - \"anyway you could showcase or prototype that motion for me?\"\n   - \"slow then down a bit\"\n   - \"yup I like c better\"\n   - \"okay cool. btw with all this new designs and redesigning the whole ui wdyt about adding some of this or something similar to this or even maybe made from scratch https://github.com/Glass-HQ/liquid-glass just because why not we yoloing anyway right and i just thought it was cool\"\n   - Standing constraints from AGENTS.md:\n     - Don't commit artifacts.\n     - Don't write to the live library.\n     - Don't spawn agents unless asked.\n     - Mockups only, no app code changes.\n     - Performance first, with no continuously repainting animations because they peg the GPU (the mascot is the exception).\n     - Local-first: no calls home.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Answer the user's liquid-glass question with an opinion and recommendation.\n   - Optionally offer to mock up a glass treatment in Paper or as an HTML prototype.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just fetched the liquid-glass repo page and was about to give my opinion. Points to make:\n   - **Fit with the app:** it would technically work, since Electron is Chromium with WebGPU, React 19 is required, and it's MIT licensed.\n   - **Risks:**\n     - The library is at version 0.0.2.\n     - Live WebGPU refraction of content underneath is expensive and repaints whenever the content moves, which conflicts with the AGENTS.md performance and GPU rules.\n     - The warm, matte, calm resurf direction could clash with heavy glass.\n   - **Suggestion:** use glass sparingly, on the floating elements that sit over content (search bar, zoom pill, toasts, maybe the open detail panel's chrome), rather than everywhere. Prefer a cheap CSS version: `backdrop-filter` blur plus a subtle highlight and border, or a static SVG displacement. Keep WebGPU refraction as an optional experiment.\n   - **Offer:** prototype one or two glass elements in HTML, or as a Paper variant of the search bar or zoom pill.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Reply in text to the user's question \"wdyt about adding some of this or something similar to this or even maybe made from scratch https://github.com/Glass-HQ/liquid-glass\". Give the recommendation above and offer to prototype a glass treatment on the floating elements. Don't make Paper or code changes until the user confirms.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"c2cfa7e1-3339-4c4e-b386-47909d3c2f1d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:40:59.913Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":34},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
