{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"c8a670d4-2ed6-4649-8be7-e617354167a0","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:43:39.246Z","version":"2.1.303","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"393849d7c89755282473547105e9b0e84221e1094921669c601bb40892e020c7","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"low"}},"base":"49e19019-fd3e-4a57-9ccf-ad0317480ef5","keep":11,"tail":["2539b5d259040820b4c006599740956bd17ce38c2121b1e7b70cfee13cc00da9","a1cd7fabe65b3d1ac57e21da27310277a8fdf58bf2664048df7339895b61e1d1","810b11ad1592013fbccee508ea06bb53916c09be8adfc6938d66ac48dc89db9c"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",13,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"539faf3fcae9a0fe4efe9db3980ca27f3237310df31a04aca5d07a78e83cf2b9"}
{"parentUuid":"f5394aae-f3b2-44ac-8e2c-8e7ea42f8869","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBY6nanq3n7XVJwodNCn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the Glass-HQ research, I'm noting that liquid-dom relies on an experimental Chrome flag for HTML-in-Canvas rendering, which is a dead end, while Plasma UI merges panels with SDF on a single canvas, liquidGL just falls back to backdrop-filter, and archisvaze's SVG+backdrop approach with an IOR-based displacement map validates my own plan and gives me solid math to reference.\n\nStudio is useful for tuning superellipse shapes and dispersion effects, but Fluidglass relies on continuous fluid simulation animation, which rules it out for my purposes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5613,"cache_read_input_tokens":41880,"output_tokens":1298,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":204},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5613,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1298,"cache_read_input_tokens":41880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5613,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5613},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9410,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBY6nJRck22AGbcAVfy7","requestRef":"c8a670d4-2ed6-4649-8be7-e617354167a0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"81ab6f5a-a069-4fe4-8460-5f15eb384262","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:43:50.347Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"81ab6f5a-a069-4fe4-8460-5f15eb384262","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBY6nanq3n7XVJwodNCn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I read all eight. Most of them confirm my earlier take, but four are interesting for different reasons.\n\n## Ruled out\n- **electron-liquid-glass:** it's macOS 26 only, and on Windows its calls do nothing. Some of its features use private Apple APIs the author labels \"DO NOT USE IN PROD\".\n- **LiquidGlassReference:** it's not a library. It's one README about Apple's iOS 26 Liquid Glass in SwiftUI, which the author wrote so Claude has the docs when building glass. There's nothing in it for the web.\n- **fluidglass:** it runs a fluid simulation (Navier-Stokes plus reaction-diffusion). That's a demo that animates all the time, the exact thing AGENTS.md bans. It also has no license.\n- **liquid-dom:** this one surprised me. It copies the live page into the GPU using Chrome's experimental HTML-in-Canvas API, which is behind `chrome://flags`. It's the technically \"correct\" way to refract live content, so it's worth watching, but no user has that flag on. It also needs React 19 and WebGPU.\n\n## Interesting\n- **liquidGL:** it bends a snapshot of the page, not the live page. Scrolling works through sync hooks, but you have to register anything that changes (`registerDynamic()`), and CSS animations don't refresh the snapshot. Images also need permissive CORS headers. Our card grid has lazy loading, hover effects and new cards arriving from capture, so it would show stale content. The useful part: its last fallback is plain `backdrop-filter`, so even the authors treat CSS as the safety net.\n- **plasma-ui:** it has the best idea in the batch. One shared WebGL canvas draws every panel, and panels touching each other merge like liquid. It has a `freezeOnScroll` option and caps panels at 16. Still, the README says it's GPU-heavy, every pass covers the full viewport, it's pre-1.0, and it doesn't run well on mobile. That's too heavy for an app that's mostly a scrolling grid.\n- **liquid-glass-studio:** a playground, not a package. It's a good reference for tuning: superellipse shapes, dispersion (colour fringing at the edges), Fresnel glare, and \"blob\" merging. I'd use the online demo to pick our values.\n- **archisvaze/liquid-glass:** ⭐ this is the approach I suggested. An SVG `feDisplacementMap` inside `backdrop-filter`, with the displacement map computed from a real refractive index, so the edge distortion is physically plausible rather than a random wobble. It's MIT licensed, plain HTML/JS, and works only in Chromium, which is all Electron needs. It also has a WebGL version.\n\n## What I'd do now\nBuild our own small `<Glass>` component, using **archisvaze's displacement math** with **values tuned in liquid-glass-studio**. It costs nothing when nothing moves, needs no canvas or snapshot, and adds no dependency. Keep plasma-ui's merging panels as an idea for later, for example the search bar and filter chips merging together.\n\nWant me to build the HTML prototype now? It would put the search bar and zoom pill over a scrolling card grid, with sliders for refractive index, blur and rim."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5613,"cache_read_input_tokens":41880,"output_tokens":1298,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":204},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5613,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1298,"cache_read_input_tokens":41880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5613,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5613},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgBY6nJRck22AGbcAVfy7","requestRef":"c8a670d4-2ed6-4649-8be7-e617354167a0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a568f8f3-f9b5-4531-948b-a73cc1e9fec7","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:43:54.039Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"t3/redesign-resurf-inspired-ui","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
