{"parentUuid":"711ef21a-ae7a-4d7a-bd18-b725b0a3763f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBYrGSYkYHegWoTYTYXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user prefers fluidglass for realism and wants a quick liquid-dom prototype. Since Electron controls the browser, I can enable the needed Chrome flag directly via the command line switch, likely something like `enable-blink-features` with `CanvasDrawElement`, making liquid-dom feasible in that environment.\n\nFor the fluidglass look, the realism comes mainly from the glass shader itself—thick refraction and specular highlights—while the fluid sim provides constant animation, so I could apply the shader's appearance to static shapes and only run the sim during interaction.\n\nFor a quick liquid-dom prototype, spinning up a full Vite+React scratch project feels heavy; instead I'm considering a minimal Electron app with a tiny main.js that opens a plain HTML page importing liquid-dom from esm.sh, with the right Chromium flag passed in. I want to check liquid-dom's README to confirm the exact flag name and core API before proceeding.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2054,"cache_read_input_tokens":47493,"output_tokens":746,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":463},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2054,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":746,"cache_read_input_tokens":47493,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2054},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_b