{"parentUuid":"9c7f2315-ca19-450f-b0bb-d1a48badac49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBa9bufuBJp45i9FEoxD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The jank spacing suggests it's tied to rasterization boundaries, roughly every 600px, possibly because content inside a canvas subtree gets rasterized synchronously rather than through compositor tiles, forcing the whole scroller image to be redrawn. I'm thinking about shrinking the snapshot region instead of capturing the full viewport backdrop.\n\nBut liquid-dom needs the backdrop as an Html node, so that complicates things. One idea is keeping the real grid as normal compositor-scrolled DOM and cloning just a tiny backdrop for the glass, though that adds complexity. To isolate the cause, I want to test whether removing images from the cards eliminates the jank — if it does, that confirms image rasterization is the bottleneck, so I'll try running it with a no-image flag.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":91976,"output_tokens":957,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":366},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":91976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7173,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBa9bXLiKFjtesky4yUU","requestRef":"20409d9b-f3b1-4831-8cc7-3073607919a3","requestedModel":"claude