{"parentUuid":"f8c23d3c-8fdb-4f00-996a-ea4ea06d34c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBcSnGxPDqcq5y2ZYknm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right. The glass was brightening and saturating whatever sat behind it, so over light photos like the mountain or the book card it looked like light-mode glass.\n\nI changed all seven glass controls across the three frames:\n- **Tint:** much darker, a near-black at 62% where it was 38%.\n- **Background:** whatever shows through is now darkened (70% brightness, which was 110%) and less saturated.\n- **Edges:** the rim highlight is about half as bright, and the inner shadow at the bottom is deeper.\n\n**5.1 Library**\n![5.1 Library with darker glass](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\glass51d.jpg)\n\n**5.2 Search**\n![5.2 Search bar with darker glass](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\glass52d.jpg)\n\n**5.3 Item**\n![5.3 Item view with darker glass](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\glass53d.jpg)\n\nI've only reviewed the 5.2 search frame closely. Over the bright mountain photo it now reads as dark glass, with the image as a dim blur underneath. 5.1 and 5.3 use the same settings, but I haven't looked at those exports myself yet. If anything still looks too light, it'll be over the brightest photos."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":501,"cache_read_input_tokens":178665,"output_tokens":490,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":501,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":178665,"c