{"parentUuid":"0a6a829c-e91e-47c0-895f-44051dc8eb1f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBkQBKtW38bCaXhm2CUY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"5.3 now has your 2.1 inspector: Spaces and tags on one \"Belongs to\" row, and the same note and details. The title over the image sits in the same dark glass pill as the library toolbar, so it stays readable on any photo.\n\n**On \"⋯\" and \"×\":** you're right to question \"⋯\". I didn't design it with specific actions in mind. Whatever it would hold (open original, copy, show in folder, archive) has a better home, so I'd drop it and spread those actions out:\n\n- **Inspector action bar:** it already has star, folder and trash. \"Open original\" (↗) and \"Copy\" fit next to them, so every item action sits in one place.\n- **Right-click the image:** a context menu with copy image, copy link, show in folder and archive. People expect this on a visual library, and it adds nothing visible.\n- **\"×\":** remove it as a button. Esc closes, and the back pill already takes you back to the grid. If you want something visible, the \"Info · Similar\" tab row could hold a quiet \"Close\" text link on the right instead of a round button.\n\nThat leaves the toolbar with just the back/forward pill and the title pill, with no small round buttons. Should I mock that up on 5.3 (and 2.1 and 2.2)?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198,"cache_read_input_tokens":72683,"output_tokens":521,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":119},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":198,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":72683,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198,"cache_creation":{"eph