{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"212bdd56b26b1f3b18b487cc0893e137d9d2dd0b69e25ad3cf259bde3e1810d4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice the grid node didn't actually get created, and the pixels look blocky like visible JPEG compression artifacts—roughly 8x8 blocks—so I'm trying to estimate the actual pixel size on screen to see if it would align with a 24px grid.\n\nCalculating based on the asset width of 3024px, the pixel scale comes out closer to 9.5px, so I'm reconsidering the grid at 16px with a correspondingly scaled width and height instead. I want to reposition the view proportionally to roughly match where the roofline sits in the original image, but tweak it to land near a more visually interesting edge, like a lantern corner, rather than a flat roof section—I'll also make sure to add a child element to the grid node so it doesn't get dropped as empty again.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017eMG81a1Xg2fySyjpJ9JTA","name":"mcp__paper__update_styles","input":{"fileId":"01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW","updates":[{"nodeIds":["9ED-0"],"styles":{"width":"48384px","height":"64512px","left":"-16400px","top":"-6000px"}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015kJrgdgGZQ5SBHYKfwwwNz","name":"mcp__paper__write_html","input":{"fileId":"01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW","targetNodeId":"9EC-0","mode":"insert-children","html":"<div data-name=\"Pixel grid\" style=\"position:absolute;left:0px;top:0px;width:100%;height:100%;background-image:linear-gradient(to right, rgba(255,255,255,0.08) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255,255,255,0.08) 1px, transparent 1px);background-size:16px 16px;background-position:-16400px -6000px;pointer-events:none\"><span style=\"opacity:0\"> </span></div>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HmMrfzpVhv4ZkP68BZ8PFs","name":"mcp__paper__get_screenshot","input":{"fileId":"0