{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"c5f1ef533d092b903c2b22036d724720fc2809c19f82e16fa1b39a0bef85626d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should design the task for haiku subagents to clean up each artboard: renaming layers semantically, removing hidden/dead nodes, switching to flex layouts over absolute positioning where feasible, and applying tokens — all without any visual change. I need to verify before/after screenshots and split the work by artboard groups to run in parallel, while watching for the risk of concurrent edits colliding in shared areas.\n\nI'm grouping the artboards into clusters (1.x, 2.x, 3.x/4.1), setting aside the duplicate 5.x set as a question to flag rather than clean automatically. I also need to flag that deleting hidden spacer elements could shift layout if surrounding elements rely on flex grow/space-between — so I should instruct agents to only remove hidden nodes if the visual result matches exactly after comparison.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll split the cleanup across three Haiku agents, one per section, so they don't touch the same screens."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XxCbGuPFsbZnEtD49mvKau","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Clean up §1 library/search screens","model":"haiku","prompt":"You are cleaning up the layer structure of Paper design mockups so they're easy to implement in code later. NO visual changes allowed.\n\nPaper file id: 01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW, page id: p-6-0 (\"resurf redesign\"). Always pass fileId and pageId.\nFirst call get_guide({topic:\"paper-mcp-instructions\"}) and read it.\n\nYour artboards ONLY (do not touch any other artboard; other agents are editing them concurrently):\n- \"1.1 Library\" (3YC-0)\n- \"1.2 Search · drops in\" (437-0)\n- \"1.3 Search · query pinned\" (484-0)\n\nSteps:\n1. get_screenshot of each artboard first and keep them as the \"before\" reference.\n2. get_tree_summary / get_jsx to inspect. Then clean up:\n   - Rename layers with generic names (\"Frame\", \"SVG\", \"Path\", \"Rect\", \"Circle\", text-derived names on containers) to clear semantic names like the existing convention: \"Toolbar\", \"Search pill\", \"Button · back\", \"Icon · search\", \"Space row · Kitchen\", \"Edge tab\". Use rename_nodes with updates:[{nodeId,name}].\n   - Delete dead nodes: nodes with visibility hidden or display none (e.g. old toolbar title text hidden behind the new glass \"Search pill\"), empty frames, and scrim/overlay nodes that are hidden. BEFORE deleting a hidden node that sits in a flex row, check if removing it would shift siblings (e.g. a space-between toolbar). If it would, either leave it or replace the layout so the result is pixel-identical; verify by screenshot.\n   - Where a raw hex color exactly equals a token, switch to the token var: --library-accent #B0714F, --library-border #262221, --library-canvas #0C0C0B, --library-muted #8D867C, --library-surface #161412, --library-surface-raised #1B1917, --library-text #E5DDD2, --app-background #0A0A09, --library-frame #0D0C0B, --library-text-soft #C9C1B6, --nav-label-active #F0E9DF. Only exact matches.\n   - Do not restructure working layouts just for style; do not change sizes, spacing, glass styles, images or text content.\n3. update_styles format: updates:[{nodeIds:[...], styles:{...}}]. Never set the \"background\" shorthand.\n4. get_screenshot of each artboard after, compare with before. If anything moved or changed, fix it.\n5. Call finish_working_on_nodes when done.\n\nReport back briefly: per artboard, what you renamed (counts), what you deleted (names), token swaps, and confirm before/after screenshots match. Do not show raw node ids except in the report."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016UwSUhB2US3vECB9ED1uoU","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Clean up §2 item view screens","model":"haiku","prompt":"You are cleaning up the layer structure of Paper design mockups so they're easy to implement in code later. NO visual changes allowed.\n\nPaper file id: 01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW, page id: p-6-0 (\"resurf redesign\"). Always pass fileId and pageId.\nFirst call get_guide({topic:\"paper-mcp-instructions\"}) and read it.\n\nYour artboards ONLY (do not touch any other artboard; other agents are editing them concurrently):\n- \"2.1 Item · Resurf-style inspector\" (4D5-0)\n- \"2.2 Item · Resurf-style · Similar tab\" (5PB-0)\n- \"2.3 Item · zoomed in, pixel grid\" (9C8-0)\nAlso leave the sticky note \"Note · Pixel zoom\" alone.\n\nKnown dead nodes: each item toolbar has a hidden \"Button · more\" (visibility hidden) that only exists to keep the centered title in place in a space-between row. 2.3 also has a hidden title text behind a glass \"Title pill\". If you remove those, you must keep the title exactly centered (e.g. make the title absolutely centered, or give left and right groups flex:1). Verify with screenshots.\n\nSteps:\n1. get_screenshot of each artboard first as the \"before\" reference.\n2. get_tree_summary / get_jsx to inspect. Then clean up:\n   - Rename layers with generic names (\"Frame\", \"SVG\", \"Path\", \"Rect\", text-derived names on containers) to clear semantic names like the existing convention: \"Toolbar\", \"Title pill\", \"Button · open original\", \"Button · show in folder\", \"Button · archive\", \"Close\", \"Pixel grid\", \"Edge tab\", \"Icon · chevron\". Use rename_nodes with updates:[{nodeId,name}].\n   - Delete dead nodes (visibility hidden / display none, empty frames) only when the result stays pixel-identical.\n   - Where a raw hex color exactly equals a token, switch to the token var: --library-accent #B0714F, --library-border #262221, --library-canvas #0C0C0B, --library-muted #8D867C, --library-surface #161412, --library-surface-raised #1B1917, --library-text #E5DDD2, --app-background #0A0A09, --library-frame #0D0C0B, --library-text-soft #C9C1B6, --nav-label-active #F0E9DF. Only exact matches.\n   - Do not change sizes, spacing, glass styles, images, image positions or text content. Do not touch the huge zoomed image in 2.3 except to rename it.\n3. update_styles format: updates:[{nodeIds:[...], styles:{...}}]. Never set the \"background\" shorthand.\n4. get_screenshot of each artboard after, compare with before. If anything moved or changed, fix it.\n5. Call finish_working_on_nodes when done.\n\nReport back briefly: per artboard, renamed counts, deleted names, token swaps, and confirm before/after match."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YK2JHa4GEFpdeLuvPRvSDr","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Clean up §3/§4 screens","model":"haiku","prompt":"You are cleaning up the layer structure of Paper design mockups so they're easy to implement in code later. NO visual changes allowed.\n\nPaper file id: 01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW, page id: p-6-0 (\"resurf redesign\"). Always pass fileId and pageId.\nFirst call get_guide({topic:\"paper-mcp-instructions\"}) and read it.\n\nYour artboards ONLY (do not touch any other artboard; other agents are editing them concurrently):\n- \"3.1 Settings · Library\" (4XI-0)\n- \"3.2 Settings · Archive\" (551-0)\n- \"4.1 Mascot · search bar travel + states\" (4RN-0)\n\nKnown dead nodes: the settings toolbars have a hidden title text (\"Everything\", visibility hidden) behind a glass \"Search pill\". If you remove it, keep the pill and the toolbar groups exactly where they are; verify with screenshots.\n\nSteps:\n1. get_screenshot of each artboard first as the \"before\" reference.\n2. get_tree_summary / get_jsx to inspect. Then clean up:\n   - Rename layers with generic names (\"Frame\", \"SVG\", \"Path\", \"Rect\", \"Circle\", text-derived names on containers) to clear semantic names like the existing convention: \"Toolbar\", \"Search pill\", \"Settings nav row · Archive\", \"Icon · close\", \"Edge tab\", \"Mascot · eyes\". Use rename_nodes with updates:[{nodeId,name}].\n   - Delete dead nodes (visibility hidden / display none, empty frames) only when the result stays pixel-identical.\n   - Where a raw hex color exactly equals a token, switch to the token var: --library-accent #B0714F, --library-border #262221, --library-canvas #0C0C0B, --library-muted #8D867C, --library-surface #161412, --library-surface-raised #1B1917, --library-text #E5DDD2, --app-background #0A0A09, --library-frame #0D0C0B, --library-text-soft #C9C1B6, --nav-label-active #F0E9DF. Only exact matches.\n   - Do not change sizes, spacing, glass styles, images or text content.\n3. update_styles format: updates:[{nodeIds:[...], styles:{...}}]. Never set the \"background\" shorthand.\n4. get_screenshot of each artboard after, compare with before. If anything moved or changed, fix it.\n5. Call finish_working_on_nodes when done.\n\nReport back briefly: per artboard, renamed counts, deleted names, token swaps, and confirm before/after match."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
