{"parentUuid":"7d5f2e83-465e-4d70-902b-6f5528477db7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBnjNmUdZsznEgaKUwwX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M4XoW96pjRwMBqwfwDsSdX","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a6ba8ab661b59e2ef","summary":"Add glass check to §2","message":"Extra task: make sure every floating control on your artboards uses the dark liquid glass. In 2.1 and 2.2 that means the back/forward pill and the zoom pill. The toolbar title should become a glass \"Title pill\" exactly like the one in 2.3: an absolutely centered pill, 34px tall, radius 17, padding 0 16px, with the title in 13px weight 600 var(--library-text). Copy it from 2.3. It does not mean the sidebar, the inspector, or the open-state edge tab (solid #0D0C0B). Use this exact recipe where glass is missing:\nbackgroundColor rgba(12,11,10,0.62); backdropFilter blur(18px) saturate(140%) brightness(0.7); borderTop 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); borderLeft and borderRight 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); borderBottom 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04); boxShadow inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.10), inset 0 -8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.5).\nGlass is a deliberate visual change here, so 2.1 and 2.2 will differ from \"before\" in those controls only. Everything else must stay identical. For reference you can look at (but not edit) \"5.3 Item · glass\" (903-0). Do not depend on it; it will be deleted after you finish. In your report, list which controls got glass.","type":"message","recipient":"a6ba8ab661b59e2ef","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Extra task: make sure every floating control on y…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2268,"cache_read_input_tokens":138139,"output_tokens":1708,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requ