{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"380dc67c0b7a7417646e04558e7be6f85fb9e34260de3cd69b8bc085558eea5b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XaF5RcnesdrqgtFzzj6cM9","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ab50d30e17353e678","summary":"Add glass check to §1","message":"Extra task: make sure every floating control on your artboards uses the dark liquid glass. That means the back/forward pill, view toggle pill, the search pill or open search bar, and any other floating pill or round control over content. It does not mean the solid \"Add\" button, the sidebar, or the open-state edge tab (solid #0D0C0B). Most already have it; apply it only where it's missing. Use this exact recipe:\nbackgroundColor rgba(12,11,10,0.62); backdropFilter blur(18px) saturate(140%) brightness(0.7); borderTop 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); borderLeft and borderRight 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); borderBottom 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04); boxShadow inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.10), inset 0 -8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.5). An active segment gets backgroundColor rgba(255,255,255,0.08).\nFor reference you can look at (but not edit) \"5.1 Library · glass\" (8PG-0) and \"5.2 Search · glass\" (8UM-0). Those are the glass versions of 1.1 and 1.2. Do not keep anything that depends on them; they will be deleted after you finish. In your report, list which controls got glass."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M4XoW96pjRwMBqwfwDsSdX","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a6ba8ab661b59e2ef","summary":"Add glass check to §2","message":"Extra task: make sure every floating control on your artboards uses the dark liquid glass. In 2.1 and 2.2 that means the back/forward pill and the zoom pill. The toolbar title should become a glass \"Title pill\" exactly like the one in 2.3: an absolutely centered pill, 34px tall, radius 17, padding 0 16px, with the title in 13px weight 600 var(--library-text). Copy it from 2.3. It does not mean the sidebar, the inspector, or the open-state edge tab (solid #0D0C0B). Use this exact recipe where glass is missing:\nbackgroundColor rgba(12,11,10,0.62); backdropFilter blur(18px) saturate(140%) brightness(0.7); borderTop 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); borderLeft and borderRight 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); borderBottom 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04); boxShadow inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.10), inset 0 -8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.5).\nGlass is a deliberate visual change here, so 2.1 and 2.2 will differ from \"before\" in those controls only. Everything else must stay identical. For reference you can look at (but not edit) \"5.3 Item · glass\" (903-0). Do not depend on it; it will be deleted after you finish. In your report, list which controls got glass."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PBMhwdeqQ6hhA7cLPcbzon","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a197150175ca4260f","summary":"Add glass check to §3/§4","message":"Extra task: make sure every floating control on your artboards uses the dark liquid glass. That means the toolbar pills behind the settings modal (back/forward, view toggle, search pill), and the search bar in the 4.1 mascot screen if it represents the floating search bar. It does not mean the settings modal panels, the sidebar, solid buttons, or the open-state edge tab (solid #0D0C0B). Apply glass only where it's missing, with this exact recipe:\nbackgroundColor rgba(12,11,10,0.62); backdropFilter blur(18px) saturate(140%) brightness(0.7); borderTop 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); borderLeft and borderRight 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); borderBottom 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04); boxShadow inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.10), inset 0 -8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.5). An active segment gets backgroundColor rgba(255,255,255,0.08).\nGlass is a deliberate change in those controls only; everything else must stay identical. In your report, list which controls got glass."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
