{"parentUuid":"98bbcc2b-a791-41d2-82cd-eb0f7184f523","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBrWaGdYnBi2SDtqYHs1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm laying out the structure: the app background, a 232px sidebar with no border, and a content well framed with rounded left corners sitting over it, plus an edge tab attached at the top that toggles between open and closed glass states. Now I'm defining the design tokens for background, frame, and radius, then starting on the app-shell component.\n\nFor the edge tab, it replaces the old sidebar-close and sidebar-toggle buttons with a single absolutely positioned button that shifts between sitting outside the frame (open) and inside it with glass styling (closed). I'm working out a flip animation using rotateY, where the shape swaps invisibly at the 90-degree edge-on point so the transition reads as a smooth 3D flip rather than a jarring state change.\n\nActually it's one continuous rotation from 0 to 180 around the edge, with content swapping at 90 degrees — I can implement this as two keyframe phases with perspective applied to the parent for the 3D effect. Now I want to check whether a keyboard shortcut already exists for this toggle, so I should look at the sidebar header JSX and surrounding lines for existing patterns.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":195571,"output_tokens":1274,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1097},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":786,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1274,"cache_read_input_tokens":195571,"cache_creation_input_tokens":786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":