{"parentUuid":"5b965063-7462-4c00-84a6-6934d908af95","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBrYFJvh8V5iFvgcGNpP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm deciding to keep mobile behavior unchanged while making the edge tab desktop-only: on desktop widths I'll hide the sidebar-close and sidebar-toggle controls and show the edge tab instead, while mobile continues using the existing drawer close button and toggle.\n\nFor positioning, since main-content clips overflow, I need to move the edge tab to be a child of app-shell instead, positioned using a CSS variable for sidebar width so it slides with the sidebar's open/closed transition. I'm aligning its vertical position with the capture bar's center and checking it doesn't conflict with Electron's draggable titlebar region.\n\nNow I'm sketching the React component: it tracks a \"shown\" state and animation phase, syncing to the open/closed prop so toggling runs an out-then-in animation (skipped under reduced motion), and wiring up the button with appropriate ARIA attributes.\n\nI'm also catching an edge case where toggling back mid-animation still resolves correctly, and realizing I need a reduced-motion fallback since `onAnimationEnd` won't fire if animations are disabled, which would leave the phase stuck—so I'll use a near-zero animation duration instead.\n\nChecking App.tsx to confirm which arrow icons from HugeIcons are already imported there.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":199940,"output_tokens":1521,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1148,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"outpu