{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"d31a5f32244ec986cbb1dc3c0899b6b2747527f90889e0cdb85691c8849eb08b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm defining the design tokens for background, frame radius, and sidebar width, then applying desktop-specific styles for the app shell, sidebar borders, and main content background.\n\nI'm also placing a small edge tab at the sidebar's right boundary with rounded corners and a shadow, sized to overlap the frame border by a pixel so it visually attaches to the panel, with smooth transition on position when toggled.\n\nWriting flip animations...\n\nWorking through the trigonometry, I find that matching the rotation angles between the open and closed tab positions requires the closed tab's angle to equal the open tab's offset minus 90 degrees, keeping the rotation continuous as it passes the edge-on point.\n\nSo I'll give each state its own flip angle via a CSS variable—open tabs use +90deg, closed tabs use -90deg—and build keyframes that animate rotateY from zero to that variable value for the outward flip.\n\nBut I realize the tab's left position is a problem: since it's calculated statically relative to sidebar width, it won't track the sidebar's actual width as it animates during open/close. I think the fix is to tie the tab's position to an isOpen-based class rather than side, so it transitions smoothly alongside the sidebar's width change.\n\nAdding edge-position and margin classes...\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HbFVXQ4gYu3GJwbUyLAu2R","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\App.tsx","old_string":"      className={`edge-tab ${side ? \"is-open\" : \"is-closed glass\"} ${phase === \"idle\" ? \"\" : `flip-${phase}`}`}","new_string":"      className={`edge-tab ${isOpen ? \"at-sidebar\" : \"\"} ${side ? \"is-open\" : \"is-closed glass\"} ${phase === \"idle\" ? \"\" : `flip-${phase}`}`}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018GaYbSJ7Y2CgGGcPTt8uXM","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\App.css","old_string":"  --glass-fill:","new_string":"  --app-background: #0a0a09;\n  --library-frame: #0d0c0b;\n  --frame-radius: 16px;\n  --sidebar-width: 248px;\n  --glass-fill:"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
