{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"fd34aaec687defe302d5bf77a72a177147face60ee2ed11160efb37b76270f4b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm replacing the sidebar's hardcoded width with a CSS variable, setting it to 220 on smaller screens via the media query, then adding edge-tab styles after the toggle rules plus a desktop frame media query for widths above 781px.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UoV3gwTPjU2dAaU3zhK3yB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\np='src/App.css';s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=\"\"\".sidebar {\n  top: 0;\n  z-index: 30;\n  width: 248px;\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,a.replace(\"248px\",\"var(--sidebar-width)\"))\nb=\"\"\"  .sidebar {\n    width: 220px;\n  }\n  .main-content {\n    width: calc(100vw - 220px);\n  }\"\"\"\nassert s.count(b)==1; s=s.replace(b,\"\"\"  :root {\n    --sidebar-width: 220px;\n  }\n  .main-content {\n    width: calc(100vw - var(--sidebar-width));\n  }\"\"\")\nc=\"\"\".mobile-menu,\n.sidebar-scrim {\n  display: none;\n}\"\"\"\nassert s.count(c)==1\ns=s.replace(c,c+\"\"\"\n.edge-tab {\n  display: none;\n}\n@media (min-width: 781px) {\n  .app-shell {\n    background: var(--app-background);\n  }\n  .sidebar {\n    border-right-color: transparent;\n    background: transparent;\n  }\n  .main-content {\n    border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n    border-right: 0;\n    border-radius: var(--frame-radius) 0 0 var(--frame-radius);\n    background: var(--library-frame);\n  }\n  .sidebar-close,\n  .sidebar-toggle {\n    display: none;\n  }\n  .edge-tab {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 44px;\n    left: 0;\n    z-index: 32;\n    display: grid;\n    place-items: center;\n    width: 26px;\n    height: 34px;\n    color: var(--library-muted);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    transition:\n      left 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n      color 0.18s ease;\n  }\n  .edge-tab:hover {\n    color: var(--ink);\n  }\n  .edge-tab.at-sidebar {\n    left: var(--sidebar-width);\n  }\n  /* Open: a solid tab hanging off the frame's edge over the sidebar. */\n  .edge-tab.is-open {\n    --flip: 90deg;\n    margin-left: -25px;\n    border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n    border-right: 0;\n    border-radius: 14px 0 0 14px;\n    background: var(--library-frame);\n    box-shadow:\n      -6px 0 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35),\n      inset 1px 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);\n    transform-origin: right center;\n  }\n  /* Closed: a glass tab just inside the frame. */\n  .edge-tab.is-closed {\n    --flip: -90deg;\n    border-left: 0;\n    border-radius: 0 14px 14px 0;\n    transform-origin: left center;\n  }\n  .edge-tab.flip-out {\n    animation: edge-tab-out 220ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 1, 1) forwards;\n  }\n  .edge-tab.flip-in {\n    animation: edge-tab-in 280ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);\n  }\n}\n@keyframes edge-tab-out {\n  from {\n    transform: perspective(300px) rotateY(0deg);\n  }\n  to {\n    transform: perspective(300px) rotateY(var(--flip));\n  }\n}\n@keyframes edge-tab-in {\n  from {\n    transform: perspective(300px) rotateY(var(--flip));\n  }\n  to {\n    transform: perspective(300px) rotateY(0deg);\n  }\n}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  /* Still fire animationend so the tab settles on its new side. */\n  .edge-tab.flip-out,\n  .edge-tab.flip-in {\n    animation-duration: 1ms;\n  }\n}\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\nbunx biome check src/App.css src/App.tsx 2>&1 | tail -8","description":"Add frame and edge tab CSS, run Biome"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
