{"parentUuid":"bebd1e1a-1365-4f5f-8b05-ec56c6d5d9d5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBrgpfr2q2eru8kBhjzR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The frame and the edge tab are working in the preview. Both steps are still uncommitted on `feat/glass-surface`.\n\n**Sidebar open:** the content now sits in a framed box with rounded left corners, and the solid tab hangs off the frame's edge over the sidebar.\n\n![Sidebar open](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\step2-open.png)\n\n**Sidebar closed:** the tab turns into a small glass tab just inside the frame.\n\n![Sidebar closed](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\step2-closed.png)\n\n- **The flip:** on a click, the tab turns edge-on over the frame's edge in 220ms, swaps sides, then turns back in over 280ms, as in the prototype. The tab rides along with the sidebar while it opens or closes. If reduced motion is on, it just switches sides.\n- **What it replaces:** the old close button in the sidebar header and the toggle in the search row. Both are hidden on desktop widths.\n- **Phones (under 781px):** nothing changes. The drawer and its own buttons work as before, with no frame and no tab.\n- **Checks:** Biome passes on both files. In the preview I clicked the tab closed and open again, and it settled on the correct side both times.\n\nMy automated checks can't show how smooth the flip feels. Please click the tab yourself at `localhost:5173`, where the preview server is still running.\n\nI haven't moved the search bar yet. The toolbar row only changes in step 3, when the full-width search bar becomes the centered glass pill. Shall I go ahead with step 3, or tweak the tab first?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":235528,"output_tokens"