{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"a3f59bac9f9608e49e96615e76e874516078d85f9de3fe1753d7562f7540741b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I shouldn't commit since the user didn't ask for that, so I'll keep working on the same branch and move to step 3: building a resting search pill with a glass effect, magnifier icon, and label like \"Everything\" or the space name, centered, that expands into the existing search bar on click or \"/\" press.\n\nFor the minimal implementation, I'll reuse the same label/input element and add an `is-resting` state class when the search isn't focused and the query is empty, showing a title span instead of the input. For the width morph, auto-width isn't animatable, so I'm considering using `interpolate-size: allow-keywords` to transition between `fit-content` and a fixed max-width like `min(700px, 100%)`, which should be supported given Electron 44's Chromium version.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the capture-bar layout: making it position relative with the search field centered via margin auto and the Add button absolutely positioned to the right, plus reconciling the resting vs open heights (settling on roughly 40px rest, 50px open). I also need to verify how clicking the label or pressing \"/\" focuses the input to trigger the open state, and check whether Escape key handling already exists to close/blur the search.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Moving on to step 3: the resting glass pill that grows into the search bar. First I'm checking how the search input handles focus, Escape and the \"/\" shortcut today."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CqhmiwsYPxFgoK8qizoSGo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"searchRef\\|\\\"Escape\\\"\\|isSearchFocused\" src/App.tsx | head -30; grep -n \"activeSpace\\b\\|const activeSpace =\\|activeView ===\\|viewTitle\\|const pageTitle\" src/App.tsx | head -12","description":"Find search focus and escape handling"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
