t with React Bits CountUp (#167)\nb8f29c9 feat(onboarding): animate the welcome and open straight onto it (#168)\nb8097c4 feat(onboarding): first-run flow (#163)\n95e7e92 fix(library): use React Bits GradualBlur for both library edges (#162)\n62afb36 fix(ingestion): capture first, enrich in the background (#166)\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"8f9886c0-1731-43fc-bd0c-2a926ad0862f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"date","date":"2026-10-19"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"67b32d34-952d-4445-8339-2edcf6af49a0","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:41:23.113Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nToday's date is 2026-10-19.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"67b32d34-952d-4445-8339-2edcf6af49a0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"09087f36-ccc3-4fd3-8c7f-071015f796dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Paper mockups (done).**\n     - Resurf-inspired redesign in file `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page `p-6-0`, using dark liquid glass.\n     - Item view decisions:\n       - Inspector copied from 2.1, with a \"Belongs to\" row.\n       - \"Close\" with an esc hint replaces ×.\n       - No \"⋯\" button.\n       - Action bar: star, move to Space, open original, show in folder, archive, then trash on the right.\n       - No context menu.\n       - The user wanted show in folder kept (\"wait show in folder is fine my bad\").\n     - Screen 2.3 added: pixel zoom with a grid, plus a sticky note.\n     - Haiku agents cleaned up the layers.\n     - The §5 glass screens were deleted after the glass check.\n   - **Building the screens in the app.** The user said \"go\", then \"yes\", then \"okay the flip is good, continue\".\n   - **Agreed order:**\n     1. Glass utility\n     2. App shell: frame + edge tab\n     3. Search pill morphing into the search bar\n     4. Item view\n     5. Settings\n     6. Pixel zoom\n   - **Back/forward pill:** the user said \"leave it out for now, add it as a final step or something\".\n   - **Deferred to later:** detail views for other item types, missing states (processing, failed), and the archived item view.\n   - **Process:** check each step in preview with the demo data and show the user a screenshot before any PR. Don't commit or open a PR unless asked.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Stack:** Electron, React, TypeScript, Vite, Bun 1.4.2. `bun run dev` serves preview on port 5173 with seed data.\n   - **Glass recipe:**\n     - fill `rgba(12,11,10,0.62)`\n     - filter `blur(18px) saturate(140%) brightness(0.7)`\n     - borders: top 0.16, sides 0.08, bottom 0.04 (white alpha)\n     - three-layer box-shadow\n   - **Frame:** `--library-frame #0d0c0b`, `--app-background #0a0a09`, `--frame-radius 16px`.\n   - **Edge tab flip:** two-phase `rotateY` (out 220ms to `var(--flip)`, swap, in 280ms). `--flip` is +90deg when open and −90deg when closed. Position follows `isOpen`; shape follows the drawn side.\n   - **Search morph:** `interpolate-size: allow-keywords` lets width transition between `fit-content` and `min(700px, 100% - 220px)`.\n   - **AGENTS.md constraints:**\n     - No pattern kills; stop only PIDs or tasks you started.\n     - Never write to the live library.\n     - No hardcoded ports or paths.\n     - Performance first; no continuously repainting animations.\n     - Commit or PR only when asked.\n     - Don't spawn agents unless asked.\n     - Screenshots go to `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\`.\n     - Run only targeted Biome checks, not repo-wide checks.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`src/App.css`**\n     - `:root` additions:\n       ```\n       --app-background:#0a0a09; --library-frame:#0d0c0b; --frame-radius:16px; --sidebar-width:248px; interpolate-size: allow-keywords; --glass-fill:rgba(12,11,10,0.62); --glass-filter: blur(18px) saturate(140%) brightness(0.7); --glass-active: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\n       ```\n     - `.sidebar` width now uses `var(--sidebar-width)`. In the `@media (max-width:1120px)` block, `:root{--sidebar-width:220px}` and `.main-content{width:calc(100vw - var(--sidebar-width))}`.\n     - `.card-video-badge`: removed its own background and backdrop-filter; it uses the `glass` class instead.\n     - After `.mobile-menu,.sidebar-scrim{display:none}`:\n       - `.edge-tab{display:none}`.\n       - `@media (min-width:781px)`:\n         - `.app-shell`: background `var(--app-background)`.\n         - `.sidebar`: transparent background and border.\n         - `.main-content`: framed with border, no right border, radius `var(--frame-radius) 0 0 var(--frame-radius)`, background `var(--library-frame)`.\n         - `.sidebar-close` and `.sidebar-toggle`: `display:none`.\n         - `.edge-tab`: absolute, top 44px, left 0, z-index 32, 26×34, grid, muted colour, `transition: left .3s`.\n         - `.edge-tab.at-sidebar`: `left: var(--sidebar-width)`.\n         - `.edge-tab.is-open`: `--flip:90deg`, `margin-left:-25px`, solid frame styles, radius `14px 0 0 14px`, `transform-origin: right`.\n         - `.edge-tab.is-closed`: `--flip:-90deg`, `border-left:0`, radius `0 14px 14px 0`, `transform-origin: left`.\n         - `.flip-out` and `.flip-in` animations.\n       - Keyframes `edge-tab-out` and `edge-tab-in` use `perspective(300px) rotateY(...)`.\n       - Reduced motion sets `animation-duration: 1ms` so `animationend` still fires.\n     - At the end of the file (glass utility moved here so it wins over component rules):\n       ```\n       /* Search: ... */ .capture-bar{justify-content:center;align-items:center;min-height:50px}\n       .capture-bar .add-button{position:absolute;top:0;right:0}\n       .capture-bar .search-field{flex:0 1 auto;width:min(700px,100% - 220px);transition: width/height/padding .32s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)}\n       .search-rest{display:none}\n       .capture-bar .search-field.is-resting{width:fit-content;height:40px;padding:0 16px 0 13px;border-radius:20px;cursor:pointer}\n       .search-field.is-resting .search-rest{display:inline-flex;gap:8px;color:var(--library-text);font-size:13px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap} svg opacity .55\n       .search-field.is-resting input, kbd, .field-mascot {position:absolute;width:0;opacity:0;pointer-events:none}\n       @media (max-width:780px){ .capture-bar .search-field{width:auto;flex:1} .capture-bar .add-button{position:static} }\n       /* Dark liquid glass ... */ .glass{border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.16);border-bottom-color:rgba(255,255,255,.04);background:var(--glass-fill);box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.1), inset 0 -8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.3), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.5);backdrop-filter:var(--glass-filter)}\n       ```\n   - **`src/App.tsx`**\n     - Imports: added `ArrowLeft01Icon` and `ArrowRight01Icon` from `@hugeicons/core-free-icons`.\n     - Badge: `<span className=\"card-video-badge glass\">`.\n     - New component before `function App()`:\n       ```tsx\n       function SidebarEdgeTab({ isOpen, onToggle }: { isOpen: boolean; onToggle: () => void }) {\n         const [side, setSide] = useState(isOpen);\n         const [phase, setPhase] = useState<\"idle\" | \"out\" | \"in\">(\"idle\");\n         useEffect(() => { if (isOpen !== side && phase === \"idle\") setPhase(\"out\"); }, [isOpen, side, phase]);\n         return (<button type=\"button\"\n           className={`edge-tab ${isOpen ? \"at-sidebar\" : \"\"} ${side ? \"is-open\" : \"is-closed glass\"} ${phase === \"idle\" ? \"\" : `flip-${phase}`}`}\n           aria-label={isOpen ? \"Close navigation\" : \"Open navigation\"} aria-expanded={isOpen} aria-controls=\"library-navigation\"\n           onClick={onToggle}\n           onAnimationEnd={() => { if (phase === \"out\") { setSide(isOpen); setPhase(\"in\"); } else setPhase(\"idle\"); }}>\n           <HugeiconsIcon icon={side ? ArrowLeft01Icon : ArrowRight01Icon} size={14} /></button>);\n       }\n       ```\n     - Rendered after `</aside>`:\n       ```tsx\n       <SidebarEdgeTab isOpen={isSidebarOpen} onToggle={() => setIsSidebarOpen((open) => !open)} />\n       ```\n     - Search label:\n       - className `search-field glass${isSearchFocused?\" is-mascot\":\"\"}${isSearchFocused||query?\"\":\" is-resting\"}`.\n       - New `<span className=\"search-rest\" aria-hidden>` with the Search01Icon (size 14) and `{activeSpace?.name ?? activeView}`.\n       - Input gets `onKeyDown`: on Escape, `setQuery(\"\")` and blur.\n       - kbd text changed to `esc to close`.\n       - The black `::before` wipe on focus is unchanged.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Missing dependencies:** `bun run dev` failed with \"vite not found\". Fixed with `bun install`.\n   - **Line endings:** Python writing on Windows produced CRLF and Biome failed. Fixed with `sed -i 's/\\r$//'`, then later writes used `newline=''`.\n   - **Server time limit:** the dev server was killed at the 30-minute background limit. Restarted with `timeout: 7200000` (task `b56epgayb`, log at `/tmp/inkling-dev.log`).\n   - **Preview first load:** the first load hung while dependencies were optimized. Reopening the tab fixed it.\n   - **Paper text nodes:** they can't take a background, so the title pill became a wrapper.\n   - **CSS gradient grid:** a gradient grid failed in Paper, so the grid became an SVG pattern.\n   - **Haiku glass check:** the §3/§4 agent refused the glass check because its brief said no visual changes. This was acceptable, since those screens already had glass.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Step 1:** verified computed glass styles on the video badge in preview.\n   - **Step 2:** verified the frame, open and closed states, and the flip settling on the correct side. The user approved the flip.\n   - **Step 3:** the resting pill renders as \"Everything\", centered, 132×40. On focus it grows to 700×50 with `is-mascot`. \"lanterns\" was typed via `preview_type`.\n   - **Phone widths (under 781px):** keep the old drawer and toggle.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"okay I made my preferred changes to the item detail screens and deleted what I didnt want, how it is now is how I want it, did I miss anything?\"\n   - \"oh well I modified 2.1 and 2.2, i forgot about 5.3 but the other two I made my prefered edits to so transfer them over\", with inline comments on quoted text:\n     - Glass on the title over the image: \"yeah ig you can add the glass to that too\".\n     - Small round buttons: \"any other ideas to that? i dont like the idea of a mono button, also why is there a details ... button anyway?\"\n     - Other item types: \"we can do that in a minute\".\n     - Missing states: \"we can do that later too\".\n     - Archived item: \"um im thinking about this for later\".\n   - \"yean nudge it\"\n   - \"can you mock that up here so I can see\"\n   - \"I like the close/esc in the top right, I like putting the open original and archive buttons in the bottom of the side panel, but dont like the show in folder and copy link/image buttons right now, also why did you even show a context menu, where does it open from\"\n   - \"wait show in folder is fine my bad\"\n   - \"I want to add a screen for the item view row that shows what it looks like when you zoom in really far in an image, I like this kind of look that paper already does when zoomed far in\" (with 2 images)\n   - \"leave a note of that next to the screen\"\n   - \"okay remember we ran some haiku subagents before to clean up the structure of the screens we made to optimize them before we start to implement them into the app, lets do that one more time now and then I think we can get starting making the screens in the app\"\n   - \"also get them to check and make sure everything that needs it uses the liquid glass and I think it would be safe then to remove the seperate liquid glass screens\"\n   - \"how would you suggest we start putting the screens into the app. like what order or what would be the most efficient way too\"\n   - \"go\"\n   - \"yes\"\n   - Answer to the back/forward question: \"leave it out for now, add it as a final step or something\"\n   - \"okay the flip is good, continue\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish verifying step 3:\n     - Pressing Escape clears the query and the bar returns to the pill.\n     - Blurring with a query keeps the bar open.\n     - Screenshots of the open and resting states.\n     - The mascot black-wipe effect looks acceptable over glass.\n   - Then show the user.\n   - Remaining steps:\n     - 4: item view\n     - 5: settings\n     - 6: pixel zoom\n     - Final: back/forward history\n   - Later: detail views for other item types, missing states, archived view. Optionally update the stale first frame of the 4.1 mascot spec, which still shows the old search icon.\n   - Commit or open a PR only when the user asks. The branch is `feat/glass-surface` with uncommitted steps 1–3.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Verifying step 3 (search pill → search bar) in the preview tab `tab_2_de0f87a3-...` at `localhost:5173`. The focus test returned `{cls:\"search-field glass is-mascot\", w:700, h:50}`, and `preview_type \"lanterns\"` was just sent. Biome passed on `src/App.css` and `src/App.tsx`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue step 3 verification, per the user's \"okay the flip is good, continue\":\n   - Take a snapshot with the query typed.\n   - Press Escape and confirm it returns to the \"Everything\" pill.\n   - Save screenshots to the chat-images folder.\n   - Report to the user. Note that the black mascot wipe still covers the glass when focused, and ask whether to keep it.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"55b31eba-e48e-41e6-8485-45a6ae802e34","timestamp":"2026-10-19T