{"parentUuid":"65bdd46d-0c8f-4efd-9bf5-0f6d0ffaece8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBwQ5MkCjtbBekE8rt8D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a bigger architectural shift than I thought: the mockup replaces the flying card overlay with a full-frame view where a stage panel and inspector take over from the library grid inside the frame itself. I'm thinking the smallest path is to create an ItemView component that swaps in for the grid when an item is selected, keeping the sidebar intact.\n\nBut that would drop the flight animation and lose all the overlay's existing features -- note editing, focus mode, processing states, tags, spaces, find similar, pin, forget. A safer plan is to keep the overlay component as-is but restyle it to cover the full content area, with media on the left as the stage and body content on the right as the inspector -- the flight animation could still work nicely if it animates from the card to the full frame. I need to look at how overlayWidth/position compute the destination frame, check the overlayMotion helpers, and see how App renders things and what contentAreaRef refers to.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20281,"cache_read_input_tokens":100385,"output_tokens":563,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":343},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20281,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":563,"cache_read_input_tokens":100385,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20281},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"contex