{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"4d41790ab9fa9e2b419684bfecb1a56c536ad86d516d95ddcd6a4d22dbe1babb","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm reconsidering trash versus archive semantics here—\"forget\" acts as archive with undo, while permanent delete is riskier territory. I'll scope the action bar to star/pin, move to space, open original, and archive, while flagging that show-in-folder and trash need more backend work before I can commit to including them.\n\nNow I'm sketching the layout for the expanded item view: a media stage with the overlay content, and an inspector panel alongside it with header, title, description, color swatches, tags, a details section, and the action bar—checking what fields LibraryItem actually exposes like colors and dimensions to match the mockup.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012txbopkYHdyMuYGCpdC79M","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"export type LibraryItem\\b\" -A60 src/lib/types.ts; grep -n \"expanded-overlay\\|\\.detail-\\|toolbar-\" src/App.css | head -80","description":"Inspect LibraryItem type and overlay CSS"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
