{"parentUuid":"fc8be682-dce4-432b-bf6d-910e2d45d2b5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01BrHz6fanTnmLmrB8rjFbh3","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"029f9c7d-6ec5-4434-a03c-baab40576b7b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:52:21.705Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"029f9c7d-6ec5-4434-a03c-baab40576b7b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBwcc3Z5q82dwQwAXrsN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm drafting the full component file, adding a helper to compute the frame's bounding rectangle relative to the viewport, falling back to window dimensions if the ref isn't ready yet.\n\nNow I'm writing the open-flight trigger, which captures the destination rect, bumps the flight id, and sets the flight state kind to \"open\" with the origin and destination rects, plus a variant that retargets from the dialog's current position for merging flights. For closing, I'm defining a similar state shape with the originating item, the dialog's current rect, an optional card rect to land on, and a flag for whether another open flight should follow. The animation itself uses GSAP timelines to tween the dialog's position, size, and border radius from the card's rounded corners to the frame's rectangular corners, with a quick opacity fade-in, and once settled it switches to a CSS class-based placed style instead of inline positioning.\n\nA ResizeObserver on the frame element plus a window resize listener keeps the destination rect updated whenever not actively flying, which also handles sidebar toggles that shift the main content's width and left offset. I'm also making sure the dialog's inspector hides during flights via an is-flying class, and confirming that setting flight state inside a layout effect re-renders synchronously before paint so there's no flash of an unstyled dialog frame.\n\nFor reduced-motion users, I still need to explicitly set the destination rect to the frame's position before fading in, since the grid-centered layout no longer applies automatically; closing without a card rect just does a plain fade out too. I'm keeping the escape and pointerdown handlers but adding an exclusion for edge tabs, and dropping the old scroll effect entirely.\n\nNow I'm laying out the inspector JSX — different title treatments per content kind (blockquote for quotes, h2 for notes), and detail rows showing saved date (stripped of the \"saved\" prefix), source hostname, media dimensions when both width and height exist, and the file type.\n\nI'll resolve the \"belongs to\" versus tag-row space chip discrepancy by following the JSX approach rather than the earlier mockup description, and build a \"Move to Space\" button that only appears when spaces exist, opening a popover of toggleable space chips above the action bar. I'm also wiring up the primary action buttons (read, open PDF, find similar, edit note), the close button with its escape kbd hint and conditional aria-label for edit mode, and a stage title pill shown across all content kinds.\n\nFor the actual file, I need to drop now-unused icon imports, replace the focus mode's CSS-driven \"Exit focus\" pseudo-element with a text label swap instead, and remove the copy-link feature and its state entirely before writing the final version.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":145406,"output_tokens":3701,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1703},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":145406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":20139,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBwcbcFMm3rmbe3LH9KK","requestRef":"bba5ecf8-efbe-4621-beb2-2bbdb6ed207a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b60893f-195e-474e-9484-96ec27c16e56","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:52:21.705Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"9b60893f-195e-474e-9484-96ec27c16e56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBwcc3Z5q82dwQwAXrsN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CP1NxP8LdTscLjMEjC7k3N","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python - <<'PY'\nimport re\np='src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nhead_end=s.index('type ExpandedItemOverlayProps')\nhead=s[:head_end]\n# imports\nhead=head.replace('''import {\n  AlertCircleIcon,\n  Archive01Icon,\n  ArrowUpRight01Icon,\n  BookOpen01Icon,\n  CheckmarkCircle01Icon,\n  Copy01Icon,\n  FileTextIcon,\n  Globe02Icon,\n  Loading01Icon,\n  PinIcon,\n  PlusSignIcon,\n  RotateCwIcon,\n  SparklesIcon,\n  Cancel01Icon,\n} from \"@hugeicons/core-free-icons\";''','''import {\n  AlertCircleIcon,\n  Archive01Icon,\n  ArrowUpRight01Icon,\n  BookOpen01Icon,\n  FileTextIcon,\n  FolderAddIcon,\n  Loading01Icon,\n  PlusSignIcon,\n  RotateCwIcon,\n  SparklesIcon,\n  StarIcon,\n} from \"@hugeicons/core-free-icons\";''')\nhead=head.replace('''import {\n  OVERLAY_EASE,\n  OVERLAY_FLIGHT_MS,\n  isCardTooFarOffscreen,\n  overlayMediaHeight,\n  overlayPosition,\n  overlayWidth,\n  prefersReducedMotion,\n  queryCardRects,\n  rectFrom,\n  scrollViewport,\n  type FlightRect,\n  type SourceRects,\n} from \"./overlayMotion\";''','''import {\n  OVERLAY_EASE,\n  OVERLAY_FLIGHT_MS,\n  prefersReducedMotion,\n  queryCardRects,\n  rectFrom,\n  type FlightRect,\n  type SourceRects,\n} from \"./overlayMotion\";''')\nhead=head.replace('''type OverlayDestination = { frame: FlightRect; mediaHeight: number };\n\ntype Flight =\n  | {\n      kind: \"open\";\n      id: number;\n      originCard: FlightRect;\n      originMediaHeight: number;\n      destination: OverlayDestination;\n    }\n  | {\n      kind: \"close\";\n      id: number;\n      fromItem: LibraryItem;\n      fromCard: FlightRect;\n      fromMediaHeight: number;\n      toRects: SourceRects | null;\n      thenOpen: boolean;\n    };\n\nconst OVERLAY_RADIUS = 18;\n''','''type Flight =\n  | { kind: \"open\"; id: number; from: FlightRect; to: FlightRect }\n  | { kind: \"close\"; id: number; fromItem: LibraryItem; from: FlightRect; to: FlightRect | null; thenOpen: boolean };\n\n// The settled view's corners match the library frame it covers.\nconst FRAME_RADIUS = \"16px 0px 0px 16px\";\n''')\n# replace provenance helpers\nhead=head.replace('''// Variant A (provenance row) derives its quiet metadata line from the item\n// itself: the file/media type comes from the pipeline (image extension or\n// kind), and the saved date is the item's own date. Tags render from the\n// item's tag list with an inline + Add affordance.\n''','')\nhead=head.replace('''function savedLabelFor(date: string): string {\n  return `SAVED ${date.replace(/^saved\\\\s+/iu, \"\").toUpperCase()}`;\n}\n\n// The overlay keeps two triage actions in view: a primary (read / play / open)\n// and secondary (open original / find similar). Everything after the first\n// entry renders in the secondary slot.\nfunction triageActions(item: LibraryItem, actions: ExpandedOverlayActions): OverlayAction[] {\n  const list: OverlayAction[] = [];\n  const sourceHost = hostnameForUrl(item.sourceUrl);\n  const hasReaderContent = Boolean(item.articleHtml || item.hasArticleContent);\n  const openOriginal: OverlayAction = {\n    key: \"open-original\",\n    label: sourceHost ?? item.source ?? \"Open original\",\n    icon: sourceHost ? (\n      <HugeiconsIcon icon={Globe02Icon} size={15} />\n    ) : (\n      <HugeiconsIcon icon={ArrowUpRight01Icon} size={15} />\n    ),\n    onClick: () => item.sourceUrl && window.open(item.sourceUrl, \"_blank\", \"noopener,noreferrer\"),\n    disabled: !item.sourceUrl,\n  };\n''','''// Content actions for the inspector: read, open the PDF, find similar.\n// Item housekeeping (star, Spaces, open original, archive) lives in the\n// action bar at the bottom instead.\nfunction contentActions(item: LibraryItem, actions: ExpandedOverlayActions): OverlayAction[] {\n  const list: OverlayAction[] = [];\n  const hasReaderContent = Boolean(item.articleHtml || item.hasArticleContent);\n''')\nhead=head.replace('''  if (item.sourceUrl) list.push(openOriginal);\n''','')\nassert 'Globe02Icon' not in head and 'savedLabelFor' not in head\nopen('/tmp/head.tsx','w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(head)\nPY\ngrep -n \"OverlayMedia\\b\" -A3 /tmp/head.tsx | head -5; grep -c . /tmp/head.tsx","description":"Rework overlay file header helpers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":145406,"output_tokens":3701,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1703},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":145406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CP1NxP8LdTscLjMEjC7k3N":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'PY'\nimport re\np='src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nhead_end=s.index('type ExpandedItemOverlayProps')\nhead=s[:head_end]\n# imports\nhead=head.replace('''import {\n  AlertCircleIcon,\n  Archive01Icon,\n  ArrowUpRight01Icon,\n  BookOpen01Icon,\n  CheckmarkCircle01Icon,\n  Copy01Icon,\n  FileTextIcon,\n  Globe02Icon,\n  Loading01Icon,\n  PinIcon,\n  PlusSignIcon,\n  RotateCwIcon,\n  SparklesIcon,\n  Cancel01Icon,\n} from \"@hugeicons/core-free-icons\";''','''import {\n  AlertCircleIcon,\n  Archive01Icon,\n  ArrowUpRight01Icon,\n  BookOpen01Icon,\n  FileTextIcon,\n  FolderAddIcon,\n  Loading01Icon,\n  PlusSignIcon,\n  RotateCwIcon,\n  SparklesIcon,\n  StarIcon,\n} from \"@hugeicons/core-free-icons\";''')\nhead=head.replace('''import {\n  OVERLAY_EASE,\n  OVERLAY_FLIGHT_MS,\n  isCardTooFarOffscreen,\n  overlayMediaHeight,\n  overlayPosition,\n  overlayWidth,\n  prefersReducedMotion,\n  queryCardRects,\n  rectFrom,\n  scrollViewport,\n  type FlightRect,\n  type SourceRects,\n} from \"./overlayMotion\";''','''import {\n  OVERLAY_EASE,\n  OVERLAY_FLIGHT_MS,\n  prefersReducedMotion,\n  queryCardRects,\n  rectFrom,\n  type FlightRect,\n  type SourceRects,\n} from \"./overlayMotion\";''')\nhead=head.replace('''type OverlayDestination = { frame: FlightRect; mediaHeight: number };\n\ntype Flight =\n  | {\n      kind: \"open\";\n      id: number;\n      originCard: FlightRect;\n      originMediaHeight: number;\n      destination: OverlayDestination;\n    }\n  | {\n      kind: \"close\";\n      id: number;\n      fromItem: LibraryItem;\n      fromCard: FlightRect;\n      fromMediaHeight: number;\n      toRects: SourceRects | null;\n      thenOpen: boolean;\n    };\n\nconst OVERLAY_RADIUS = 18;\n''','''type Flight =\n  | { kind: \"open\"; id: number; from: FlightRect; to: FlightRect }\n  | { kind: \"close\"; id: number; fromItem: LibraryItem; from: FlightRect; to: FlightRect | null; thenOpen: boolean };\n\n// The settled view's corners match the library frame it covers.\nconst FRAME_RADIUS = \"16px 0px 0px 16px\";\n''')\n# replace provenance helpers\nhead=head.replace('''// Variant A (provenance row) derives its quiet metadata line from the item\n// itself: the file/media type comes from the pipeline (image extension or\n// kind), and the saved date is the item's own date. Tags render from the\n// item's tag list with an inline + Add affordance.\n''','')\nhead=head.replace('''function savedLabelFor(date: string): string {\n  return `SAVED ${date.replace(/^saved\\\\s+/iu, \"\").toUpperCase()}`;\n}\n\n// The overlay keeps two triage actions in view: a primary (read / play / open)\n// and secondary (open original / find similar). Everything after the first\n// entry renders in the secondary slot.\nfunction triageActions(item: LibraryItem, actions: ExpandedOverlayActions): OverlayAction[] {\n  const list: OverlayAction[] = [];\n  const sourceHost = hostnameForUrl(item.sourceUrl);\n  const hasReaderContent = Boolean(item.articleHtml || item.hasArticleContent);\n  const openOriginal: OverlayAction = {\n    key: \"open-original\",\n    label: sourceHost ?? item.source ?? \"Open original\",\n    icon: sourceHost ? (\n      <HugeiconsIcon icon={Globe02Icon} size={15} />\n    ) : (\n      <HugeiconsIcon icon={ArrowUpRight01Icon} size={15} />\n    ),\n    onClick: () => item.sourceUrl && window.open(item.sourceUrl, \"_blank\", \"noopener,noreferrer\"),\n    disabled: !item.sourceUrl,\n  };\n''','''// Content actions for the inspector: read, open the PDF, find similar.\n// Item housekeeping (star, Spaces, open original, archive) lives in the\n// action bar at the bottom instead.\nfunction contentActions(item: LibraryItem, actions: ExpandedOverlayActions): OverlayAction[] {\n  const list: OverlayAction[] = [];\n  const hasReaderContent = Boolean(item.articleHtml || item.hasArticleContent);\n''')\nhead=head.replace('''  if (item.sourceUrl) list.push(openOriginal);\n''','')\nassert 'Globe02Icon' not in head and 'savedLabelFor' not in head\nopen('/tmp/head.tsx','w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(head)\nPY\ngrep -n \"OverlayMedia\\b\" -A3 /tmp/head.tsx | head -5; grep -c . /tmp/head.tsx","description":"Rework overlay file header helpers"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01CP1NxP8LdTscLjMEjC7k3N":{"cwd":"/c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgBwcbcFMm3rmbe3LH9KK","requestRef":"bba5ecf8-efbe-4621-beb2-2bbdb6ed207a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"87468b7d-4