{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"72230d72957db91343988050bbb8956d109c1d6fe21a701ebba40de4adc7bedc","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning the settings restyle to match the mockups: reordering tabs to Library, Archive, Browser extension with renamed labels and Library as default, and adding a sidebar footer with a privacy note plus app version, checking if the version string is already exposed somewhere in the build.\n\nFor the Library panel I'm figuring out what's feasible without backend support — computing item counts and kind breakdowns from existing data since disk size and folder access aren't available in the renderer, and laying out export/restore as rows with icon tiles and pill buttons. For Archive I'm keeping the existing card grid but restyling the header with title, subtitle, and select/close controls, and for the modal itself I need to look at the CSS to rework the sidebar and content panel styling with a larger heading.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015snE1m1CrWJmBW5o6LmWru","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 2745,2960p src/App.css; sed -n 3029,3150p src/App.css; sed -n 4975,5000p src/App.css; grep -rn \"__APP_VERSION__\\|appVersion\\|getVersion\" src --include=*.ts* | head -5","description":"Read settings CSS"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
