{"parentUuid":"b61cbbf5-6414-44f5-9706-246394d8e9ad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"df757c0a-f7cd-4adf-8c41-b5ffba2893d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Build the resurf-redesign Paper mockups (file `01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW`, page `p-6-0`) into the app, in this order:\n     1. Glass (done)\n     2. App shell (done)\n     3. Search pill (done)\n     4. Item view (done)\n     5. Settings (done, `2d901d7`)\n     6. Pixel zoom (done by Haiku, `89357b4`)\n     7. Final: back/forward history (pending)\n   - Deferred: other item-type detail views, processing/failed states, the archived item view, and the Similar tab.\n   - Draft PR https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170 is on branch `feat/glass-surface` and already linked.\n   - The user is low on money: \"get haiku 5.5 xhigh to do it\" and \"haiku pls\". Delegate work to the Agent tool with `model: haiku`, `effort: xhigh`, and keep my own work minimal.\n   - Item view closes only via the close button or Esc. No outside-click close.\n   - Phone width is out of scope.\n   - Latest request: remove the \"Web preview — sample data\" badge (\"supposed to be gone remember\"). Also remove the glass title pill over the photo stage, since it duplicates the side panel title.\n   - AGENTS.md constraints:\n     - No pattern kills.\n     - Never write to the live library.\n     - No hardcoded ports or paths.\n     - Targeted Biome and tsc only.\n     - Screenshots go to `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\`.\n     - Commits end with a Co-Authored-By line.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Electron, React, TypeScript, Vite, and Bun.\n   - The preview runs via `bun run dev` on 5173 as background task `b56epgayb`.\n   - The item view uses a GSAP flight with `.is-flying`.\n   - The Entire CLI `prepare-commit-msg` hook can hang commits.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `src/App.tsx`:\n     - Settings restyle (LibraryMakeup, tabs, archive header).\n     - The preview badge (around lines 4425–4450) is now removed in the staged changes.\n   - `src/App.css`:\n     - `.settings-panel-header .settings-close` is 32px.\n     - The archive grid uses `minmax(160px, 1fr)`.\n     - Pixel zoom CSS was added.\n     - `.item-stage-title` rules and the badge CSS were removed (staged).\n   - `src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx`:\n     - Haiku added a `ZoomableImage` component with a zoom pill (fit up to 3200%), pixelated rendering plus a grid past `PIXEL_ZOOM` = 800%, and drag-pan.\n     - The title pill div was removed (staged).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Haiku's commit hung on the Entire `prepare-commit-msg` hook. It did not bypass the hook.\n   - My retry with `timeout 60 git commit ... </dev/null` apparently did not create a commit: `git log` still shows `89357b4`, and nothing was pushed. The changes remain staged and unresolved.\n\n5. Problem Solving: The settings and pixel zoom steps are pushed. The badge and pill removal is staged but not committed.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"continue, but get haiku 5.5 xhigh to do it, im running outta money here\"\n   - [screenshot] \"that web preview badge is supposed to be gone remember, also just remove the pill over the content grid area where the photo is because it justs restates the title/name of the photo that already exists in the side panel\"\n   - \"haiku pls\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Get the staged removal commit (\"fix(library): drop the preview badge and stage title pill\", co-author Claude Haiku 5.5) made and pushed. The Entire hook is blocking it.\n   - Ask whether to skip the hook (`--no-verify` requires the user's OK).\n   - Then step 7, back/forward history, via Haiku. I asked whether to proceed and have no answer yet.\n   - Possible changelog line: ask the user.\n\n8. Current Work: Committing the staged badge and title-pill removal. The commit did not land (HEAD is still `89357b4`). Changes are staged in the worktree.\n\n9. Optional Next Step: Tell the user the removals are done and staged, but the Entire `prepare-commit-msg` hook hangs the commit. Ask whether to bypass it with `--no-verify` or have them fix Entire. Also ask whether Haiku should start back/forward history.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"436e9cd7-d47e-4b8e-bc59-eaa01f438309","timestamp":"2026-10-19T17:37:48.362Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":74},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
