{"parentUuid":"50e71253-30ce-4535-872b-b8221fc5eeee","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","description":"Needs an agent running inside a T3 thread. Delegate one task to a T3-owned child agent/subagent of THIS thread and run it with only the supplied task prompt, without copying parent conversation history. Choose providers and models from orchestrator_capabilities, which uses the same live catalog as the composer. Prefer native subagent tools for same-provider work only when they support the chosen model. Use this for any model missing from the native tool, including same-provider work, for cross-provider work, or for explicitly T3-owned child tasks. For every T3 delegated review round, call delegate_task again with the original brief, prior findings, responses, and unresolved objections in the task prompt. Track each round by its own taskId and use a distinct clientRequestId per round, stable across retries of that round. The childThreadId is backing storage, not the target for starting another delegated review round through t3_thread_send. Set isolation to worktree for a separate checkout based on the parent local commit, with project setup completed before the child starts. Uncommitted edits are not copied; omitted isolation shares the parent checkout. Provider, model, model options (see orchestrator_capabilities), runtime mode, and interaction mode inherit unless target overrides them. A requested runtimeMode must be one the target provider lists in orchestrator_capabilities runtimeModes; an inherited one steps down to the broadest mode it offers. Leave runtimeMode unset unless the user asks for a supervised child: approval-required and auto-accept-edits usually make the child wait for a person at each action that needs approval. Prefer mode='async' for long work; mode='wait' blocks until completion, a blocking question, or timeout. If hasPendingQuestion, pass threadId=childThreadId to t3_pending_request_list, t3_pending_request_read (with requestId) and t3_pending_request_respond, or ask the user; the task's completion still wakes this thread. timeoutMs on mode=wait is only the parent's wait budget and does not cancel the child. waitTimedOut on that wait call means the timeout fired; keep that taskId and read status on later task_status. An async child's completion wakes this thread through a notification, steered into active turns where supported or queued otherwise, so end the turn instead of polling or spawning watchers; use task_status only when the result is needed mid-turn.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"task":{"type":"string"},"target":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"providerInstanceId":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"driverKind":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"model":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"options":{"anyOf":[{"anyOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"value":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"boolean"}]}},"required":["id","value"],"additionalProperties":true}},{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"boolean"}]}}],"description":"Model option selections advertised by orchestrator_capabilities."},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":true},{"type":"null"}]},"title":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"role":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["implementation","research","review","design","test","general"]},{"type":"null"}]},"isolation":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["shared","worktree"],"description":"Defaults to shared: use the parent's checkout. Worktree creates a separate checkout from the parent's current local commit before starting the child. Uncommitted edits are not copied."},{"type":"null"}]},"mode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["async","wait"],"description":"Defaults to async. Use wait only when this turn needs the child's result before you can continue."},{"type":"null"}]},"timeoutMs":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Wait budget for mode=wait only. Default 10 minutes. Elapsing it returns waitTimedOut=true on that call and does not cancel the child."},"clientRequestId":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"runtimeMode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["inherit","approval-required","auto-accept-edits","auto","full-access"],"description":"Defaults to inherit; omit it unless the user asks for a supervised child. A narrower mode is not a read-only switch: on most providers, approval-required and auto-accept-edits pause the child at each action that needs approval until a person approves it in the child's thread, which this thread cannot do. To limit what the child does, say so in the task. A mode ranked above this thread's is rejected; that ranking does not promise the child's provider permissions are narrower than this thread's."},{"type":"null"}]},"interactionMode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["inherit","default","plan"]},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["task"],"additionalProperties":true},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__t3-code__orchestrator_capabilities","description":"List the V2 provider instances and their current models from the same live catalog as the composer, including configured custom models, inherited runtime settings, and app-owned orchestration features available to this caller. For a separate top-level thread in a new or existing worktree, use t3_thread_launch with workspaceStrategy.","input_schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__t3-code__task_status","description":"Needs an agent running inside a T3 thread. Read a T3-owned delegated task created by this parent thread. childRunId identifies the original delegated run. workState distinguishes working, waiting_for_children, and result_available; a completed turn with live nested work is not a completed task. summary is the final task result, including provider errors on failure, and remains stable after publication. hasPendingChildRuns reports later queued or executing turns in the backing child thread, even after the task is terminal; it does not reopen the task, and task_cancel stops those turns too. Turns held in a stopped queue wait for the user and do not count. latestTerminal* provides later non-monitor turn results. Reading a terminal result acknowledges its automatic parent delivery.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"taskId":{"type":"string"}},"required":["taskId"],"additionalProperties":true},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"efce4c5e-4dc3-45a1-8c87-cc79a19038b9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T17:47:25.659Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.303","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
