{"parentUuid":"78e4bc35-8190-4280-8834-5f7f909cf6f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC4ToM1dwo891f6PexRz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013HKLUNHKLaK8d3zhALiF1s","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). Read AGENTS.md: no pattern kills, never touch the live library, no hardcoded ports/paths, targeted Biome + tsc only.\n\nThe in-memory back/forward history in src/App.tsx (commits 05afc79, 5552965, 1026abe, db8ec0f) records the view, the Space, the search query and the open item. It does not record the \"Find similar\" results view: clicking Find similar on an item, then going Back, skips past that results screen.\n\nMake the Find similar results a history step like a search or Space, so Back and Forward land on it and restore it, along with its source item. Keep the change minimal. Don't regress the existing history behaviour, including the card flights (on- and off-screen) and the search debounce.\n\nVerify in the running preview with the T3 preview tools (port is in /tmp/inkling-dev.log; don't start another server). Go open item → Find similar → open a result → Back (similar view) → Back (previous) → Forward. Commit `feat(library): find similar joins history`, ending with `Co-Authored-By: GPT-6 Luna <noreply@openai.com>`, using `git commit --no-verify ... </dev/null` (the user approved skipping the hook), then `git push`. Report what you changed, the SHA, and the verification results.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"implementation","clientRequestId":"history-fix-r3-similar","title":"Find similar in history"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1566,"c