{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"28adc6fb285edf6327b9f26fb62f6005501130b7ef7f93d4abf90841a5f2c105","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The commit timed out silently, likely because a hook is waiting on stdin even though I redirected from /dev/null. Rather than bypass the hooks, I should ask the user how to proceed.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The preview badge and the title pill over the photo are both removed in the code, but the change isn't committed or pushed yet. A commit hook on this machine (the Entire CLI `prepare-commit-msg` hook) hangs on every commit. It hung for Haiku, and my one retry with a 60-second cutoff timed out too.\n\nThe changes are staged and pass Biome and the typecheck: 3 files, 43 lines deleted. Earlier commits on this branch went through fine, so the hook only started hanging recently.\n\nCan you either fix or restart Entire, or tell me to commit with `--no-verify` to skip the hook this once? Once it's committed and pushed, the last step is back/forward history."}]}}
