{"parentUuid":"a5acd751-9a69-4ff3-a117-ae2bafb04cc5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCTcS1YF3qJGnstSmUwQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ToD4BBYoHjGv3g19PLXAXs","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). Read AGENTS.md first. These rules are critical:\n- never kill processes by pattern;\n- NEVER open or write to the user's live library;\n- the user is running the full desktop app right now, so don't touch or close it;\n- no hardcoded ports or paths.\nYou are a TESTER. Don't change source code or commit anything.\n\nGoal: verify, in the Windows desktop app (Electron, the full backend), that \"Find similar\" is a step in back/forward history (commit 0e169c3 in src/App.tsx). The expected sequence is:\nopen an item → click Find similar → open a result → Back lands on the similar results → Back returns to where you were before → Forward brings the similar results back. Also check that the card flight animation still happens on history open/close.\n\nHow:\n1. Work out from electron/ how the app picks its library location (look for an env var, a userData override, or a CLI flag).\n2. Run the app against a SANDBOX library in a fresh temp dir outside the worktree. Seed it from the committed demo seed (public/seed-demo/ + src/seedPersonal.ts) or another documented safe way. Never point it at the real library.\n3. If there is no safe way to isolate the library, STOP and report that, with what you found. Don't run the app.\n4. Use `bun run build:dir`, or another dev path that exercises the real backend. Find similar needs embeddings, so let the background jobs finish (wait on real completion, not sleeps).\n5. Drive the app with whatever desktop/automation tooling is available.\n6. Save screenshots to C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\ (similar-history-*.png).\n7. Close only processes whose PIDs you captured at spawn.\n\nReport pass/fail per step, with repro steps for any failure and the screenshot paths.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"test","clientRequestId":"similar-history-desktop-test-r1","title":"Find similar desktop test"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2600,"cache_read_input_tokens":87543,"output_tokens":1962,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":306},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2600,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1962,"cache_read_input_tokens":87543,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2600},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ToD4BBYoHjGv3g19PLXAXs":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). Read AGENTS.md first. These rules are critical:\n- never kill processes by pattern;\n- NEVER open or write to the user's live library;\n- the user is running the full desktop app right now, so don't touch or close it;\n- no hardcoded ports or paths.\nYou are a TESTER. Don't change source code or commit anything.\n\nGoal: verify, in the Windows desktop app (Electron, the full backend), that \"Find similar\" is a step in back/forward history (commit 0e169c3 in src/App.tsx). The expected sequence is:\nopen an item → click Find similar → open a result → Back lands on the similar results → Back returns to where you were before → Forward brings the similar results back. Also check that the card flight animation still happens on history open/close.\n\nHow:\n1. Work out from electron/ how the app picks its library location (look for an env var, a userData override, or a CLI flag).\n2. Run the app against a SANDBOX library in a fresh temp dir outside the worktree. Seed it from the committed demo seed (public/seed-demo/ + src/seedPersonal.ts) or another documented safe way. Never point it at the real library.\n3. If there is no safe way to isolate the library, STOP and report that, with what you found. Don't run the app.\n4. Use `bun run build:dir`, or another dev path that exercises the real backend. Find similar needs embeddings, so let the background jobs finish (wait on real completion, not sleeps).\n5. Drive the app with whatever desktop/automation tooling is available.\n6. Save screenshots to C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\ (similar-history-*.png).\n7. Close only processes whose PIDs you captured at spawn.\n\nReport pass/fail per step, with repro steps for any failure and the screenshot paths.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"test","clientRequestId":"similar-history-desktop-test-r1","title":"Find similar desktop test"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCTcRbEie9UZqkA7RBAH","requestRef":"c578a080-322e-4f90-8ec7-d6d843205309","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"67335e91-e0bf-4813-ae25-c7a993c365cc","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:27:35.788Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
