{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"77ece0850b268f2261cd1b9e2767854be202b7d1257c0fba8da348292854eff2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking about splitting the work across multiple agents by area, having each one read the code and compare it against Paper's screenshots rather than spinning up conflicting dev servers. It's simpler to let them use the screenshot tool plus the user's existing screenshots to check shell, sidebar, grid, and other components separately.\n\nFirst, each agent needs to pull the basic info on page p-6-0 to get the list of Paper artboards, then claim their assigned area -- strictly read-only, no edits allowed.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011aK5XtQTnBaDeaZMn99WM2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit shell/grid vs Paper","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","prompt":"READ-ONLY AUDIT. Don't edit code, commit, or start or kill any servers.\n\nRepo: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). The redesign mockups are in Paper: file 01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW, page p-6-0. Load the Paper guide first: mcp__paper__get_guide({topic:\"paper-mcp-instructions\"}). Then use get_basic_info / get_tree_summary / get_screenshot / get_jsx / get_computed_styles on that page. Pass pageId so you don't disturb the user's view.\n\nYOUR AREA: the app shell. That means the window frame, sidebar (logo, nav, Spaces list, Settings/Help), header (back/forward, search pill, Add button), item count, view toggles, the card grid and EVERY card type (image, article, PDF, video, post, note, quote, file), card hover/selected states, the list view, the search results state, the empty states, the Add/capture UI, and the Space create/rename menus.\n\nFor each Paper artboard in your area, compare it against the implementation in src/App.tsx, src/App.css and src/components/ (read the code; the user's current app screenshot is at C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\userdata\\attachments\\d09afd25-cdc5-42e7-866c-f30bf652d16f-3e62c27c-30ff-43ff-af9e-85cff6b695e0.png). Use exact values from Paper (computed styles), not guesses.\n\nReturn a concise list of what's NOT done or doesn't match. Each line: screen › element › what Paper shows vs what the app does, with severity (missing / wrong / minor). Also list any Paper artboards in your area that have no implementation at all. Don't pad the list.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017YKfcq9VJMCbxYoLtbLfZL","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit item view vs Paper","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","prompt":"READ-ONLY AUDIT. Don't edit code, commit, or start or kill any servers.\n\nRepo: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). The redesign mockups are in Paper: file 01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW, page p-6-0. Load the Paper guide first: mcp__paper__get_guide({topic:\"paper-mcp-instructions\"}). Then use get_basic_info / get_tree_summary / get_screenshot / get_jsx / get_computed_styles on that page. Pass pageId so you don't disturb the user's view.\n\nYOUR AREA: the opened item view. That means the stage, inspector panel, action bar, tags, Spaces chips, details, the zoom pill, and every item-type detail view (image, article/reader, PDF, video, post, note editing, quote, file). Also the processing and failed states, the archived item view, and any Similar tab.\n\nCompare each Paper artboard in your area against src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx, src/ReaderView.tsx, src/components/*, src/App.tsx and src/App.css (read the code). Use exact values from Paper's computed styles.\n\nReturn a concise list of what's NOT done or doesn't match. Each line: screen › element › what Paper shows vs what the app does, with severity (missing / wrong / minor). Also list any Paper artboards in your area that have no implementation at all. Don't pad the list.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015FZge6C6gNEkHFQLGoiGVh","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit settings/other vs Paper","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","prompt":"READ-ONLY AUDIT. Don't edit code, commit, or start or kill any servers.\n\nRepo: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). The redesign mockups are in Paper: file 01M51FDW8EAY40ZQSN6NKJAAYW, page p-6-0. Load the Paper guide first: mcp__paper__get_guide({topic:\"paper-mcp-instructions\"}). Then use get_basic_info / get_tree_summary / get_screenshot / get_jsx / get_computed_styles on that page. Pass pageId so you don't disturb the user's view.\n\nYOUR AREA: everything that isn't the shell/grid or the opened item view. That means Settings (Library, Archive, Browser extension tabs), the archive grid and its selection mode, Help & shortcuts, onboarding/welcome, dialogs, confirmations, toasts, menus, Top of mind, Serendipity, and any other screen or artboard on that page. Start by listing ALL artboards on the page, so nothing is skipped.\n\nCompare each one against src/App.tsx, src/App.css and src/components/ (read the code). The user's current Settings screenshot is at C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\userdata\\attachments\\d09afd25-cdc5-42e7-866c-f30bf652d16f-b4ae4368-8efd-491a-ba71-c5a725098ca9.png. Use exact values from Paper's computed styles.\n\nReturn:\n(1) the full artboard list with a one-word area tag for each;\n(2) a concise list of what's NOT done or doesn't match in your area. Each line: screen › element › what Paper shows vs what the app does, with severity (missing / wrong / minor). Also list any artboards with no implementation at all. Don't pad the list.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
