{"parentUuid":"f717eb23-bfce-477f-a62b-ae223541f67a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCUQtSYwnGPeex5snsef","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Settings and other-screens audit is in. I'll wait for the main window and item view audits, then send you one combined list.\n\nOne finding affects everything, so you might want to think about it now. The Paper designs use DM Sans for headings, system-ui for body text and DM Mono for small details, but the app uses Paper Mono for all text. That alone is a big part of why it looks \"halfway done\". Was the all-mono look on purpose, or should the app switch to Paper's fonts?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4132,"cache_read_input_tokens":100146,"output_tokens":169,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4132,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":100146,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4132},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCUQshurFsQnG5b7oc7k","requestRef":"1179a3b6-98f3-47d4-bdb7-bea055f64213","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd90a2d8-600f-4f18-a161-8575075ce00b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:35:55.692Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:36:02.341Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a984058270ba51012</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_017YKfcq9VJMCbxYoLtbLfZL</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a984058270ba51012.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit item view vs Paper\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Read-only audit of the item view against Paper page \"resurf redesign\". Scope: artboards 2.1 (inspector), 2.2 (Similar tab), 2.3 (pixel zoom), the two Note artboards, and the §2 label. I compared Paper's computed styles against `ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx`, `App.tsx`, `App.css`, and `electron/thumbnail.mjs` by reading them. I did not run the app, so px values are from code, not rendered output.\n\nMatches: viewer-well background and radius, 320px inspector and padding, space chip, tag and add-tag, details label and rows, 32px action buttons, zoom pill size and glass recipe, pixel grid (8%, 1px).\n\n**Missing**\n1. 2.1 › inspector header › Info / Similar tabs (14px, Info active at 600) left of Close. App header has only Close (`ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx` 849-866). [missing]\n2. 2.2 › Similar tab body › Paper: two-column tile grid inside the inspector (139px columns, 8px gap, 12px radius, image, quote and note tiles). App has no inspector similar view. Find similar is a library-wide results mode (`App.tsx` ~3170, \"similar to\" context ~5314), triggered by a text button under Details (`ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx` 163-171). That button is not in Paper 2.1, so it's an extra control. [missing, different model]\n3. 2.1 › title block › five 22px rounded swatches below the title. App has none, and `LibraryItem` has no palette field (`types.ts` 35 has only `accent`, a card style class). Needs a color source. [missing]\n4. 2.1 › viewer toolbar › glass back/forward group (62×34) and glass centered title pill (156×34, 13px DM Sans 600). App has neither. The capture bar with back/forward sits under the overlay (`App.tsx` 4927). Back/forward still work via Alt+Arrow and mouse buttons 3/4 (`App.tsx` 4390-4396), but nothing is visible. [missing]\n5. 2.1 › action bar › Paper: favorite, move to space, open original, show in folder, archive, plus trash at the far right. App: favorite, move-to-space (only with Spaces), open original (only with a source URL), archive. No show-in-folder and no delete (`ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx` 1039-1102). Permanent delete exists only in the archive list (`App.tsx` ~1016). [missing]\n6. Liquid glass note › liquid-dom (WebGPU) glass on search bar and zoom pill › App ships only the CSS `backdrop-filter` fallback (`.glass`, `App.css` 5650). The WebGPU path isn't built. Decide whether it ships. [missing]\n\n**Wrong**\n7. All 2.x inspector text › Paper uses system-ui for title (26/30, 600, -0.025em), labels, note, chips, details; DM Mono only for size, zoom and esc. App item-view rules set no font-family, so they inherit `--font-ui: \"Paper Mono\", ui-monospace, monospace` (`App.css` 35-36). The whole inspector renders in Paper Mono. Zoom label, Size and esc also use Paper Mono where Paper uses DM Mono (`App.css` 5309, 5634; `ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx` 864). [wrong]\n8. 2.3 › zoom source › Paper's 1600% is 16 screen px per pixel of the 3024×4032 original (grid spans 48384×64512). App's `ZoomableImage` uses `item.image`, which is the thumbnail when one exists (`App.tsx` 386-387; `thumbnailEdge = 512` in `electron/thumbnail.mjs` 6). Zoom, the grid and pixelation therefore run on thumbnail pixels, about 8× coarser than the original. Zooming past fit needs the original, loaded on demand. [wrong]\n9. 2.1 › zoom label at fit › Paper shows 80%, but its displayed 470×640 image is about 16% of its stated 3024×4032. App computes fit from the displayed source, so the label is size-dependent (e.g. about 140% for a 384×512 thumbnail in a ~740px stage). Paper's 80% needs a definition before anyone matches it. [wrong, Paper inconsistent]\n10. Liquid glass note › Paper's note limits glass to search bar and zoom pill, but 2.1 also puts glass on the history group and title pill. App adds `.glass` to the closed edge tab and video badge, which the note doesn't list. [wrong, Paper inconsistent]\n\n**Minor**\n11. 2.1 › Details › Paper has three rows (Saved, From, Size). App adds Type (`ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx` 996-999).\n12. 2.1 › space chip dot › Paper: about 13×12 blob icon. App: 6px circle (`App.css` 2580).\n13. 2.1 › title position › Paper title at 66px (40px tab row + 20px gap). App at 60px (14px body padding, `App.css` 5218).\n14. 2.1 › note box › Paper min-height 72px. App has none (`App.css` 5231).\n15. 2.1 › stage image › Paper: 4px radius, box-shadow 0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,0.55). App: no radius, drop-shadow 0 24px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.5) (`App.css` 5133-5141).\n16. 2.1 › edge tab › Paper top 19px. App top 44px (`App.css` ~744). Verify in app.\n17. 2.1 › sidebar width › Paper 232px, App `--sidebar-width` 248px (`App.css` 30). Sidebar is outside my area, but it makes the item frame 16px narrower.\n\n**Artboards with no implementation or no artboard**\n- Reader/article, PDF, video, post, note editing, quote and file detail views: no artboards on this page. Only the image item is designed here. The \"screens\" page (p-3-0) has older detail artboards (article detail, Image Item Detail, footer layouts C/D/F/G, note editor flow). They're not part of the redesign, so I didn't compare them.\n- Processing and failed states: no artboard here. The text search for \"process\" and \"fail\" only matches the mascot artboard's \"Capture failed\", which is outside my area. App has `.detail-processing` and `.retry-button` (`ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx` 911-938), not compared visually.\n- Archived item view: no artboard. \"Archive\" appears only on settings artboards.\n- Inkling-style side panel: the §2 label says \"Two side panel directions, each with its similar items view. Resurf-style on the left, inkling-style on the right.\" Only Resurf-style artboards exist (2.1, 2.2), so the inkling-style direction is missing in Paper.\n\nDecision, not a mismatch: App picks 800% as the pixel-zoom threshold (`ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx` 180). The Paper note leaves it open.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>200483</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>54</tool_uses><duration_ms>466669</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
