{"parentUuid":"fb4f49f9-0db5-46ef-a147-e3f79e763060","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCUXppy8espNZaYqtMMK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should combine these into a concise, scannable list, and flag that the Paper page only has 15 artboards, meaning many app areas still lack designs.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3430,"cache_read_input_tokens":107362,"output_tokens":2222,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":43},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3430,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2222,"cache_read_input_tokens":107362,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3430},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1893,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgCUXpY6bmXskGigLEQ2F","requestRef":"37cfb597-c0af-44cd-a29c-8ccb780c5832","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"973614fe-68d4-4afa-902a-6143205e18b5","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:37:30.040Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"973614fe-68d4-4afa-902a-6143205e18b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCUXppy8espNZaYqtMMK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Haiku agents compared the code with the Paper page; none of them ran the app. You're right that it's far from done. Each list below runs from biggest gap to smallest.\n\nThe Paper page only designs these screens: Library, the two search states, the image item view (info, Similar tab and pixel zoom), Settings Library and Archive, and the mascot. Everything else in the app has no design to compare against.\n\n**Affects every screen**\n1. **Fonts:** Paper uses DM Sans for headings and labels, system text for body, DM Mono for small details and Libre Baskerville for quotes. The app uses Paper Mono everywhere. This one change accounts for most of the \"doesn't look like the design\".\n2. **Glass toolbar:** in Paper the back/forward buttons and the grid/list toggle sit in glass capsules top-left, floating over the cards, which scroll underneath. In the app, back/forward are bare buttons beside the search pill, the toggles are in a solid box on their own row, and the cards never go under the toolbar.\n3. **Grid size:** Paper has 4 columns of 286px with a 12px gap. The app makes about 6 columns of 176px with an 8px gap, so every card is smaller than designed.\n\n**Library and search (1.1–1.3)**\n- **Search with a query:** in Paper the search pill stays small and centred, the query becomes a glass chip with an ×, and \"6 results\" shows on the right. The app keeps the search bar wide open and has no chip.\n- **Article card:** it should be a cream card showing the title, site and read time. In the grid the title and site are hidden, so it looks like an untitled image.\n- **File card:** a file with no thumbnail shows as a blank tile.\n- **Quote card:** Paper shows the whole quote large with a big quote mark. The app cuts it to 2 lines, about 69 characters.\n- **Video card:** Paper has a glass pill bottom-left with a play icon and the length. The app shows a play button in the middle and the provider name instead of the length, and the app doesn't store video length at all.\n- **Note and PDF cards:** the type sizes are a bit off.\n- **Add button:** 50px tall in the app, against a 34px pill in Paper.\n- **Item count:** \"N items in library\" shows all the time. Paper only shows \"N results\", and only while searching.\n- **Sidebar:**\n  - **Width:** 248px, against 232px in Paper.\n  - **Logo:** the app adds the \"inkling\" wordmark next to the blot; Paper has the blot only.\n  - **Icons:** don't match. Paper has a dot grid, a star and a shuffle.\n  - **Row sizes:** the nav rows are bigger than Paper's.\n  - **Active row:** gets a filled background in the app; Paper has none.\n- **Space counts:** only the active Space shows its count. Paper shows a count on every Space.\n- **Space colours:** Spaces use plain dots instead of Paper's coloured blob shapes. Only orange actually shows; blue, green, pink and purple all come out grey, so changing a Space's colour looks like it does nothing.\n- **Avatar:** Paper puts one in the sidebar footer. It implies an account, which goes against keeping everything local, so you'd need to decide on it.\n\n**Item view (2.1–2.3)**\n- **Info / Similar tabs:** Paper has these at the top of the side panel. The app has neither.\n- **Similar tab:** Paper shows a 2-column grid of similar items inside the side panel. The app's \"Find similar\" replaces the whole library view instead.\n- **Glass controls on the photo:** Paper has a glass back/forward group and a title pill there. The app has neither. You asked me to remove the title pill, so that one stays gone.\n- **Colour swatches:** Paper shows 5 under the title. The app doesn't store item colours, so this needs new data.\n- **Action bar:** Paper has \"show in folder\" and delete buttons. The app has neither.\n- **Zoom quality:** zoom runs on the 512px thumbnail, not the original, so the pixel grid is about 8× coarser than designed. To fix it, the original would load when you zoom in.\n- **Small style differences:** the Details panel has an extra \"Type\" row, the photo's corners and shadow differ a little, and the title sits 6px higher.\n\n**Settings and Archive (3.1–3.2)**\n- **Archive tiles:** Paper uses even square tiles with the title and \"type · time\" underneath. The app shows the art only, with no titles.\n- **Restore button:** Paper has one on hover. The app only has a delete in the top-right corner.\n- **Library details:** Paper shows the disk size (\"2.4 GB on disk\"), a \"Show folder\" button, a \"last copy Oct 12\" line that survives restarts, and the app version. None of these exist in the app.\n- **Sidebar active row:** in the app it's a filled pill; in Paper it's just bold text.\n- **Orange ring on the close button:** the app puts focus on the close button when Settings opens. That's the ring in your screenshot, and Paper doesn't have it.\n- **Small style differences:** the background dimming, padding and font sizes are a little off.\n- **Browser extension tab:** it has no Paper design. In the app it shows a raw \"Listening on 127.0.0.1:port\" line, and renewing uses the browser's built-in confirm box.\n\n**Mascot (4.1):** the movement between the sidebar and the search bar should take 0.38s in Paper. The app moves it at 0.7–2.4s, but nobody has watched it run.\n\n**Liquid glass:** Paper's note recommends WebGPU glass for the search bar and zoom pill. The app only has the plain CSS blur version.\n\n**Screens in the app with no design on this Paper page:** Top of mind, Serendipity, list view, empty states, the Add menu, Space creation and its menus, Help & shortcuts, onboarding, toasts, the archive's multi-select mode, the processing and failed states, the archived item view, and the item views for articles, PDFs, video, posts, notes, quotes and files. A separate Paper page has onboarding, toasts and archive multi-select designs, but nobody checked them.\n\nCalls I need from you:\n1. Switch to Paper's fonts, or keep the all-mono look?\n2. Avatar in the sidebar: yes or no?\n3. Should the Similar tab replace the \"Find similar\" results view?\n4. Should colour swatches and video length get stored?\n5. Should zoom load the original image?\n\nThe Luna \"Find similar\" test and the PR screenshots are still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3430,"cache_read_input_tokens":107362,"output_tokens":2222,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":43},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3430,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2222,"cache_read_input_tokens":107362,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3430},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCUXpY6bmXskGigLEQ2F","requestRef":"37cfb597-c0af-44cd-a29c-8ccb780c5832","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5bd3f5c4-752d-4e0e-9105-46bd45425966","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:37:48.693Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
