{"parentUuid":"9db0db8c-28e7-4828-8ea5-24f576899cbd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCXUSJeh9rQoEEYFheiN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014GrQtfAkZ1D5UXqCHDs6No","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). Read AGENTS.md: no pattern kills, never touch the live library, no hardcoded ports/paths, targeted Biome + tsc only. The user may have the desktop app open, so don't touch processes you didn't start.\n\nBug found in a desktop test of the back/forward history in src/App.tsx (commits 05afc79, 5552965, 1026abe, db8ec0f, 0e169c3).\n\nRepro: open \"Spider-Man in the rain\", choose Find similar, open \"Eye lenses\", then press Back twice. Both Backs work: the first lands on the similar results, the second on the source item. But Forward is then DISABLED, and the similar results can't be reached again.\n\nLikely cause: restoring the history entry (leaving similar mode, reopening the source item) fires a state change that pushes a new entry and truncates the forward stack. Fix it so restoring an entry never pushes. Check the same thing for every restore path: view, Space, search query (including the 600ms debounce firing after a restore), open item, and similar mode.\n\nAdd a focused bun test if the history logic can be tested without rendering. If it's all component state, extract the small pure stack logic only if that's trivial; otherwise skip the test.\n\nVerify in the web preview: start `bun run dev` yourself in the background, capture its PID, read the port from its output, and stop only that PID afterwards. Check Back×N then Forward×N round-trips across a view change, a Space, a search and an open item. Find similar needs the desktop backend; the tester sandboxed it with Electron's `--user-data-dir` and the demo seed. Reuse that if it's cheap, otherwise reason it through the code.\n\nCommit `fix(library): restoring history keeps forward entries`, ending with `Co-Authored-By: GPT-6 Luna <noreply@openai.com>`, using `git commit --no-verify ... </dev/null`, then `git push`. Report the cause, the fix, the SHA and the verification.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"implementation","clientRequestId":"history-fix-r4-forward","title":"History forward truncation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3024,"cache_read_input_tokens":116206,"output_tokens":1037,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3024,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1037,"cache_read_input_tokens":116206,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3024},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014GrQtfAkZ1D5UXqCHDs6No":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface). Read AGENTS.md: no pattern kills, never touch the live library, no hardcoded ports/paths, targeted Biome + tsc only. The user may have the desktop app open, so don't touch processes you didn't start.\n\nBug found in a desktop test of the back/forward history in src/App.tsx (commits 05afc79, 5552965, 1026abe, db8ec0f, 0e169c3).\n\nRepro: open \"Spider-Man in the rain\", choose Find similar, open \"Eye lenses\", then press Back twice. Both Backs work: the first lands on the similar results, the second on the source item. But Forward is then DISABLED, and the similar results can't be reached again.\n\nLikely cause: restoring the history entry (leaving similar mode, reopening the source item) fires a state change that pushes a new entry and truncates the forward stack. Fix it so restoring an entry never pushes. Check the same thing for every restore path: view, Space, search query (including the 600ms debounce firing after a restore), open item, and similar mode.\n\nAdd a focused bun test if the history logic can be tested without rendering. If it's all component state, extract the small pure stack logic only if that's trivial; otherwise skip the test.\n\nVerify in the web preview: start `bun run dev` yourself in the background, capture its PID, read the port from its output, and stop only that PID afterwards. Check Back×N then Forward×N round-trips across a view change, a Space, a search and an open item. Find similar needs the desktop backend; the tester sandboxed it with Electron's `--user-data-dir` and the demo seed. Reuse that if it's cheap, otherwise reason it through the code.\n\nCommit `fix(library): restoring history keeps forward entries`, ending with `Co-Authored-By: GPT-6 Luna <noreply@openai.com>`, using `git commit --no-verify ... </dev/null`, then `git push`. Report the cause, the fix, the SHA and the verification.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"implementation","clientRequestId":"history-fix-r4-forward","title":"History forward truncation"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCXUS2XhQnyARPh9zEbx","requestRef":"4b8a4409-f328-4726-b7bd-ffedde412880","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"t3-code","attributionMcpTool":"task_status","type":"assistant","uuid":"12483b1f-ed28-4245-a624-548be1fcece4","timestamp":"2026-10-20T00:16:11.571Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktr