{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"3c20732d-32c2-4eda-9ccb-dcea92bfa8f4","timestamp":"2026-10-20T00:16:12.657Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"9fbed77dab96867d53aa6af93e3452b26af3d8d6ac1dc102b9bbcdf8fac9a669","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"low"}},"base":"4b8a4409-f328-4726-b7bd-ffedde412880","keep":114,"tail":["f545caa0e27e48b709f0ec8f281d3aae41af7f737333f868bfe86f664f79b827","9278094e42c9f53c7c15fff1c41fec69e2b236ff7d07276a6cebb8f811e8c816","87c9e9cf348bd114c8d1601a83e540a6da5118bd4097d162ada471e96df7b673"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",116,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"2f83243d22105600ce57958445f011795f87add2e561aec049a33013928c8ce5"}
{"parentUuid":"49a1c0e4-e3e0-4966-885c-a38f23868ff0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCXVEUHVZmJx9xBk1Hsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The desktop test of \"Find similar\" in back/forward found a bug, and I've sent the fix to a GPT-6 Luna on high. Luna ran the test against a separate test library made from the demo data, not your real one.\n\n**What works:** open an item, click \"Find similar\", open a result, and Back takes you to the similar results. Back again takes you to the item you started from. The card animation plays on each step.\n\n**What fails:** after those two Backs, Forward is greyed out, so you can't get back to the similar results. Most likely, going back to the starting item gets recorded as a brand-new step, which wipes out everything ahead of it. Luna is fixing that for every kind of step, not just Find similar.\n\n**Not yet checked:** while an item is open, the item view seems to cover the toolbar's back button. Luna couldn't click it with the mouse and had to trigger it in code. This connects to a gap from the Paper comparison: the design has its own glass back/forward buttons on the item view. It'll get fixed whenever those buttons are built. Until then, the mouse side buttons and Alt+Left/Right still work.\n\nThe five design questions from the gap list are still open."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1537,"cache_read_input_tokens":119230,"output_tokens":371,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1537,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":371,"cache_read_input_tokens":119230,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1537,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_t